WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:34.368
<i>You know this story.</i>

2
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.008
<i>The crack of lightning.</i>

3
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.548
<i>A mad genius.</i>

4
00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:54.288
<i>An unholy creation.</i>

5
00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:01.462
<i>The world, of course,
remembers the monster,</i>

6
00:01:01.495 --> 00:01:02.897
<i>not the man.</i>

7
00:01:04.832 --> 00:01:07.034
<i>But sometimes,
when you look closely...</i>

8
00:01:07.068 --> 00:01:08.903
<i>there's more to a tale.</i>

9
00:01:10.438 --> 00:01:12.440
<i>Sometimes the monster
is the man.</i>

10
00:01:20.748 --> 00:01:23.084
<i>I've been with the circus
for as long as I can remember.</i>

11
00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:27.455
<i>Circuses like to think
of themselves as families.</i>

12
00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:31.525
<i>But, of course,
each one has its clown.</i>

13
00:01:37.331 --> 00:01:38.566
Oh!

14
00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.639
<i>I didn't have a name
back then.</i>

15
00:01:44.672 --> 00:01:46.907
<i>I was just "the hunchback".</i>

16
00:01:46.941 --> 00:01:48.943
<i>Or "freak",
if you were being kind.</i>

17
00:01:51.178 --> 00:01:53.714
<i>But the truth is,
I didn't hate them for it.</i>

18
00:01:53.748 --> 00:01:55.016
<i>It's hard to judge cruelty</i>

19
00:01:55.049 --> 00:01:56.617
<i>when you've
never known kindness.</i>

20
00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:05.493
<i>Besides, I always
had someone to look up to.</i>

21
00:02:31.385 --> 00:02:32.787
<i>When I wasn't performing,</i>

22
00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.289
<i>I served
as the company's doctor.</i>

23
00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:37.491
<i>I became fascinated by
the science of medicine.</i>

24
00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:39.859
<i>Particularly of human anatomy.</i>

25
00:02:43.064 --> 00:02:45.433
<i>I wanted to understand
everything about...</i>

26
00:02:45.466 --> 00:02:49.236
<i>...this internal universe
that makes us who we are.</i>

27
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:53.274
<i>The brains, lungs,
bones, muscles.</i>

28
00:02:55.876 --> 00:02:57.144
<i>The heart.</i>

29
00:02:58.479 --> 00:03:00.181
<i>I don't know
why the science of life</i>

30
00:03:00.214 --> 00:03:02.283
<i>captured my imagination.</i>

31
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:04.757
<i>I think
it just helped me escape.</i>

32
00:03:08.356 --> 00:03:09.523
My God!

33
00:03:10.591 --> 00:03:13.894
You really think you're smart,
don't you, eh? Huh?

34
00:03:13.928 --> 00:03:15.996
A real intellectual.

35
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.732
What an embarrassment
that must be!

36
00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:20.768
Oi!

37
00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.069
You're on!

38
00:03:26.907 --> 00:03:28.175
<i>Little did I know</i>

39
00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:30.044
<i>that on a chilly
London evening...</i>

40
00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:31.412
<i>...I was about to meet the man</i>

41
00:03:31.445 --> 00:03:34.382
<i>who would change
my life forever.</i>

42
00:04:02.309 --> 00:04:05.212
Ladies and gentlemen!

43
00:04:06.847 --> 00:04:09.417
Witness now
the death-defying feats

44
00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.952
of our very own
bird in the sky...

45
00:04:11.986 --> 00:04:15.823
The beautiful Lorelei!

46
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.925
Lorelei!

47
00:04:52.893 --> 00:04:54.128
Lorelei! Lorelei!

48
00:04:55.563 --> 00:04:56.664
Oh, Lorelei!

49
00:04:57.765 --> 00:04:59.600
She can't breathe!

50
00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:01.202
Previous injuries?

51
00:05:01.235 --> 00:05:02.736
Uh, she broke her arm
a year ago

52
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.410
and her collarbone
sometime before that.

53
00:05:05.005 --> 00:05:07.408
Oh! Oh, my God.

54
00:05:08.209 --> 00:05:09.877
Collarbone
is rebroken,

55
00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.645
shoulder's dislocated,
causing pressure on the lungs.

56
00:05:11.679 --> 00:05:12.780
She can't breathe.

57
00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:13.814
What do we do?

58
00:05:13.848 --> 00:05:15.082
Nothing, I'm afraid.

59
00:05:15.116 --> 00:05:16.716
Don't have the tools
to reset the bone.

60
00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.889
Do you have a pocket watch?
Give it to me.

61
00:05:21.922 --> 00:05:23.802
I'm not giving you...
Do this now or she dies!

62
00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:28.162
Come on!

63
00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.133
Wait.

64
00:05:35.236 --> 00:05:37.071
That dislocation is
forcing the sternum

65
00:05:37.104 --> 00:05:38.472
to rest at an
untenable angle, yes?

66
00:05:38.506 --> 00:05:40.140
Yes. Ready?
Set?

67
00:05:40.174 --> 00:05:42.443
Three, two, one...

68
00:05:46.347 --> 00:05:47.507
Yes!
There we are.

69
00:05:50.217 --> 00:05:52.253
You saved me.
Breathe.

70
00:05:52.286 --> 00:05:53.486
Thank you.

71
00:05:54.288 --> 00:05:55.489
That was incredible.

72
00:05:55.523 --> 00:05:57.491
Why are you wearing
that silly makeup?

73
00:05:57.525 --> 00:05:58.959
Well, I'm a clown.
You're not a clown,

74
00:05:58.993 --> 00:06:00.528
you're a physician...

75
00:06:00.561 --> 00:06:01.896
...who just performed
a dry surgery

76
00:06:01.929 --> 00:06:03.864
in less than a minute
with nothing to prepare.

77
00:06:03.898 --> 00:06:05.432
Well, I'm a clown physician.

78
00:06:05.466 --> 00:06:06.734
Don't panic,
ladies and gentlemen!

79
00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:08.335
All part of the act!

80
00:06:09.803 --> 00:06:10.905
You're being wasted here.

81
00:06:13.407 --> 00:06:14.975
I'm with the circus, sir.

82
00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:17.049
You're going to
leave the bloody circus.

83
00:06:17.144 --> 00:06:18.546
What's going on?

84
00:06:19.246 --> 00:06:20.581
You're a doctor, then?

85
00:06:20.614 --> 00:06:22.383
On my better days.

86
00:06:22.416 --> 00:06:24.084
Chiswick Cross Hospital
is just up the road.

87
00:06:24.118 --> 00:06:25.553
I can lead your men there now.

88
00:06:27.621 --> 00:06:28.889
Get her out of here sharpish!

89
00:06:28.923 --> 00:06:30.724
Go out the back way.

90
00:06:30.758 --> 00:06:32.693
Don't want her
upsetting the clientele.

91
00:06:35.896 --> 00:06:38.399
Where are they taking
that poor creature?

92
00:06:38.432 --> 00:06:40.834
Sir! Please,
may I know your name?

93
00:06:51.712 --> 00:06:53.948
Ladies and gentlemen!

94
00:06:54.815 --> 00:06:56.717
The Human Cannonball!

95
00:07:04.692 --> 00:07:06.260
Please, no!

96
00:07:06.293 --> 00:07:08.128
You sneaky rat!

97
00:07:08.162 --> 00:07:10.664
You want to leave? I own you!

98
00:07:10.698 --> 00:07:12.533
I've had enough
of these books!

99
00:07:12.566 --> 00:07:14.768
You belong to the circus!
Burn them!

100
00:07:14.802 --> 00:07:16.503
Please, Master Barnaby,
it's my only thing.

101
00:07:17.871 --> 00:07:20.074
No! No!

102
00:07:20.107 --> 00:07:21.542
Get out of there!

103
00:07:22.543 --> 00:07:24.545
Let that be a lesson to you!

104
00:07:25.112 --> 00:07:26.413
Get in there!

105
00:07:26.447 --> 00:07:27.948
You are going nowhere!

106
00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:33.687
Do you know
what's happened to Lorelei?

107
00:07:39.927 --> 00:07:41.829
Romanticizing, are we?

108
00:07:44.365 --> 00:07:47.301
She's probably gonna die,
you know that.

109
00:07:48.636 --> 00:07:51.438
These city doctors
and their dirty hospitals.

110
00:07:54.608 --> 00:07:55.608
Ow!

111
00:08:23.437 --> 00:08:25.506
What are you doing?

112
00:08:25.539 --> 00:08:28.075
High powered magnet.
Should work. Usually does.

113
00:08:28.108 --> 00:08:29.943
Hold on, sir. You don't know
what he'll do to me.

114
00:08:29.977 --> 00:08:31.745
Don't I?
I can't just leave.

115
00:08:31.779 --> 00:08:33.614
Of course you can.
No, sir, they own me!

116
00:08:35.349 --> 00:08:37.718
You are better than this.
You can be better.

117
00:08:37.751 --> 00:08:40.287
I can get you out,
but you'll have to trust me, understand?

118
00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.656
Oi!

119
00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.810
Choose now or remain here
for the rest of your days.

120
00:08:45.826 --> 00:08:48.462
Get away from that cage!
You hear me?!

121
00:08:48.495 --> 00:08:49.563
- Open it!
- Oi!

122
00:08:51.899 --> 00:08:54.435
Get him!
He's property of the circus!

123
00:08:54.468 --> 00:08:55.736
Now, the thing is...

124
00:08:59.173 --> 00:09:00.541
He's robbed us!

125
00:09:04.978 --> 00:09:07.981
The hunchback! He's attacked
me and robbed the circus!

126
00:09:08.415 --> 00:09:09.717
Get him!

127
00:09:12.419 --> 00:09:14.054
Get after him!

128
00:09:33.173 --> 00:09:34.408
Don't touch him!

129
00:09:41.982 --> 00:09:42.982
Go!

130
00:10:16.016 --> 00:10:17.050
Got you.

131
00:10:17.885 --> 00:10:20.454
What do we do?
What do we do now?

132
00:10:26.727 --> 00:10:28.028
Oh, shit.

133
00:10:41.575 --> 00:10:43.544
How do we get out of here?

134
00:10:43.577 --> 00:10:45.479
You know this place, damn it!
How do we...

135
00:10:52.319 --> 00:10:53.487
Where are they?

136
00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:54.588
Whoa!

137
00:11:17.477 --> 00:11:18.812
I'm not in the circus.

138
00:11:18.846 --> 00:11:19.847
What?

139
00:11:21.915 --> 00:11:23.116
Yes, very good.

140
00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.718
Come along!

141
00:11:26.186 --> 00:11:28.306
I've never been
out of the circus before, sir.

142
00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.800
Eyes open, door shut.
Coat off.

143
00:11:51.511 --> 00:11:53.814
Coat off.

144
00:11:53.847 --> 00:11:56.950
We're going to slip into something
a little more comfortable.

145
00:12:14.201 --> 00:12:15.201
What's that for?

146
00:12:17.337 --> 00:12:18.906
Next order of business.

147
00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.109
No. What are you
gonna do to me?

148
00:12:28.115 --> 00:12:29.716
Absolutely nothing.

149
00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:31.752
Don't worry about it.

150
00:12:34.988 --> 00:12:35.989
Look.

151
00:12:40.093 --> 00:12:41.653
This is going to hurt
just a little bit.

152
00:12:44.564 --> 00:12:46.733
What are you doing to me?
Listen to me!

153
00:12:47.167 --> 00:12:49.136
You are not...

154
00:12:49.636 --> 00:12:50.938
...a hunchback.

155
00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:56.843
Not a real one, anyway. No.

156
00:12:56.877 --> 00:12:58.679
You have an abscess...

157
00:12:58.712 --> 00:13:00.814
causing a fluid pocket,
a rather...

158
00:13:01.415 --> 00:13:03.884
...large fluid sac.

159
00:13:03.917 --> 00:13:05.452
It hurts!

160
00:13:05.485 --> 00:13:07.120
Yes, I imagine it does.

161
00:13:07.154 --> 00:13:08.834
You'd be surprised
how often I hear that.

162
00:13:17.531 --> 00:13:18.999
Oh, looking at the size
of this beauty,

163
00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:20.672
I'd say it's gone
untreated for, oh...

164
00:13:20.701 --> 00:13:22.970
...18 years, but...

165
00:13:23.003 --> 00:13:24.304
...the good news is,
I'm convinced

166
00:13:24.338 --> 00:13:26.218
that if we can drain it...

167
00:13:27.407 --> 00:13:29.376
...in three...

168
00:13:30.277 --> 00:13:31.277
...two...

169
00:13:31.878 --> 00:13:33.680
...one. And pulling out.

170
00:13:38.852 --> 00:13:40.654
<i>Garde a l'eau!</i>

171
00:13:43.223 --> 00:13:44.223
Right.

172
00:13:44.791 --> 00:13:45.959
That's the easy part done.

173
00:13:45.993 --> 00:13:46.994
Easy part?

174
00:13:51.832 --> 00:13:53.066
You're all right!

175
00:13:54.034 --> 00:13:56.737
And up... we... go.

176
00:13:57.871 --> 00:14:00.073
Now, your muscles...

177
00:14:00.774 --> 00:14:02.409
...your bones...

178
00:14:02.442 --> 00:14:05.045
...your entire
skeletal system...

179
00:14:05.078 --> 00:14:08.415
...will be struggling
to reset themselves...

180
00:14:08.448 --> 00:14:11.618
...to return you to
your former ground-sniffing...

181
00:14:11.651 --> 00:14:14.454
...Luddite-bearing posture
of the last...

182
00:14:14.488 --> 00:14:15.655
...18 years.

183
00:14:15.689 --> 00:14:17.891
So, for the time being,
my friend,

184
00:14:17.924 --> 00:14:19.793
you shall have to
wear this rather...

185
00:14:19.826 --> 00:14:22.095
...wonderful back brace
I constructed for Gordon.

186
00:14:22.429 --> 00:14:23.429
Who?

187
00:14:25.832 --> 00:14:27.701
I'm standing up!

188
00:14:27.734 --> 00:14:29.136
That's rather obvious.

189
00:14:29.169 --> 00:14:31.171
I haven't overestimated
your intelligence, have I?

190
00:14:31.204 --> 00:14:32.506
It's just I'm not
in the circus

191
00:14:32.539 --> 00:14:33.539
and now I'm standing up.

192
00:14:34.241 --> 00:14:35.442
Yeah, you said that.

193
00:14:35.475 --> 00:14:37.077
Right!

194
00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.446
Library and study are over
there. Kitchen's over there.

195
00:14:39.479 --> 00:14:40.947
I'm standing up.

196
00:14:40.981 --> 00:14:42.249
Your bedroom's on the right.

197
00:14:42.282 --> 00:14:44.551
There's a water heater
and soap in there.

198
00:14:44.584 --> 00:14:47.120
I suggest you use it
to do something about your...

199
00:14:47.754 --> 00:14:49.489
...hair.

200
00:14:49.523 --> 00:14:51.391
I'll be in the basement for
the rest of the evening,

201
00:14:51.425 --> 00:14:53.193
as I have school...

202
00:14:53.226 --> 00:14:54.528
...in the morning.
Make yourself at home,

203
00:14:54.561 --> 00:14:55.729
don't touch anything.

204
00:14:56.096 --> 00:14:57.664
Oh!

205
00:14:57.697 --> 00:15:00.534
By the way, I had,
have a flatmate.

206
00:15:00.567 --> 00:15:02.469
Goes by the name
of Igor Straussman.

207
00:15:02.502 --> 00:15:03.570
Man's a morphine addict.

208
00:15:03.603 --> 00:15:04.905
Idiot. Complete liar.

209
00:15:04.938 --> 00:15:06.273
Thankfully for us,
he's almost...

210
00:15:06.306 --> 00:15:07.974
...never home.

211
00:15:08.008 --> 00:15:10.544
So, should anyone question
your presence here,

212
00:15:10.577 --> 00:15:11.937
you are to say
that you are he.

213
00:15:12.512 --> 00:15:13.512
I'm Igor?

214
00:15:13.847 --> 00:15:14.915
Very good.

215
00:15:19.886 --> 00:15:21.822
"Hello, my name is Igor."

216
00:16:40.734 --> 00:16:41.968
Let's see.

217
00:16:42.002 --> 00:16:44.104
A dangerous hunchback is

218
00:16:44.137 --> 00:16:46.606
detained for the safety
of the public...

219
00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.109
...with a determined and
equally dangerous accomplice.

220
00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.246
They proceed
to the circus owner's trailer,

221
00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.782
where they rob the safe
of its contents.

222
00:16:55.815 --> 00:16:57.984
They make their violent
escape, culminating...

223
00:16:58.018 --> 00:16:59.452
...in the murder
of an innocent man,

224
00:16:59.486 --> 00:17:00.620
and vanishing...

225
00:17:02.656 --> 00:17:04.124
...into thin air.

226
00:17:07.127 --> 00:17:08.929
A fair summing up, Alistair?

227
00:17:08.962 --> 00:17:10.864
Yes, Inspector.

228
00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:13.600
Escape, robbery, murder.

229
00:17:14.734 --> 00:17:16.403
Just as Mr. Barnaby said.

230
00:17:29.549 --> 00:17:31.549
Now here's what
I think happened, Alistair.

231
00:17:32.285 --> 00:17:34.888
A human being
with a spinal deformity

232
00:17:34.921 --> 00:17:37.123
is locked up against his will.

233
00:17:39.059 --> 00:17:41.261
Perhaps a common feature
of his treatment here.

234
00:17:42.796 --> 00:17:44.231
A stranger releases him...

235
00:17:45.031 --> 00:17:46.666
...using a magnet
and tickler...

236
00:17:47.901 --> 00:17:49.502
...as any fool can.

237
00:17:50.604 --> 00:17:54.074
They make their escape
urgently, as they must...

238
00:17:54.107 --> 00:17:55.675
...for the circus
is against them.

239
00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:58.011
They flee.

240
00:17:58.778 --> 00:18:00.247
A chase.

241
00:18:01.581 --> 00:18:03.016
A man dies.

242
00:18:05.719 --> 00:18:08.521
Manslaughter in self-defense
at most, I would say.

243
00:18:34.848 --> 00:18:36.850
"Wanted for murder."
Have it copied.

244
00:18:36.883 --> 00:18:37.784
I thought you said it wasn't...

245
00:18:37.817 --> 00:18:38.817
I did.

246
00:18:41.855 --> 00:18:44.224
Something tells me
our circus freak...

247
00:18:44.257 --> 00:18:46.426
may be only the beginning.

248
00:18:55.669 --> 00:18:56.736
Good morning!

249
00:19:06.212 --> 00:19:08.114
<i>Igor:
At school till six.</i>

250
00:19:08.148 --> 00:19:09.382
<i>Clothes in the wardrobe.</i>

251
00:19:09.416 --> 00:19:11.584
<i>Money and key
in the tin by the door.</i>

252
00:19:11.618 --> 00:19:13.353
<i>Be home for dinner. F.</i>

253
00:19:26.333 --> 00:19:28.234
Chiswick Hospital.

254
00:21:01.428 --> 00:21:02.896
Doctor?

255
00:21:02.929 --> 00:21:05.329
This way, gentlemen.
We have amputation to perform.

256
00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.500
You.

257
00:21:09.335 --> 00:21:11.371
What, me?
Yeah.

258
00:21:11.404 --> 00:21:13.706
She needs camphor inhalations
twice a day,

259
00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.241
uh, extract of allium...

260
00:21:15.275 --> 00:21:17.243
...a quarter ounce of arsenic
and three of Filcher's Oil,

261
00:21:17.277 --> 00:21:18.411
but more if you can get it.

262
00:21:18.445 --> 00:21:20.613
I can't do that.
You can.

263
00:21:20.647 --> 00:21:23.616
And then
when she wakes, tell her...

264
00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:25.852
...a friend will be back.

265
00:22:12.866 --> 00:22:14.167
Six months ago,

266
00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.369
a man tried to buy parts of
recently deceased animals...

267
00:22:16.402 --> 00:22:18.104
...at the London
Zoological Gardens.

268
00:22:18.138 --> 00:22:19.506
He was turned away.

269
00:22:19.539 --> 00:22:21.508
Two weeks later,
there was a forced entry.

270
00:22:21.541 --> 00:22:23.409
Animal limbs amputated
and stolen.

271
00:22:23.443 --> 00:22:25.144
A month later,
a similar pattern of events

272
00:22:25.178 --> 00:22:26.579
at the Veterinary Academy.

273
00:22:26.613 --> 00:22:28.581
Sounds gruesome,
but what...

274
00:22:28.615 --> 00:22:31.284
I confiscated that from
the crime scene at the circus.

275
00:22:31.784 --> 00:22:32.819
Open it.

276
00:22:39.959 --> 00:22:40.959
Sir...

277
00:22:43.897 --> 00:22:45.265
...this is disgusting.

278
00:22:46.733 --> 00:22:48.935
It belonged to a lioness
recently deceased.

279
00:22:51.371 --> 00:22:53.773
But it was found near our
murder victim at the circus...

280
00:22:53.806 --> 00:22:55.842
...and it didn't walk there
of its own accord.

281
00:22:57.510 --> 00:22:59.479
You think
there's a connection?

282
00:22:59.512 --> 00:23:01.180
I think our other man
at the circus

283
00:23:01.214 --> 00:23:02.694
fits the same description
as this...

284
00:23:03.016 --> 00:23:04.284
...animal thief.

285
00:23:06.452 --> 00:23:07.987
But who would do that?

286
00:23:09.055 --> 00:23:10.055
Huh?

287
00:23:12.058 --> 00:23:13.426
What motive?

288
00:23:14.928 --> 00:23:16.429
Something reeks here.

289
00:23:18.231 --> 00:23:20.433
It reeks of an evil,
sinful mischief.

290
00:23:20.466 --> 00:23:22.602
And now that man walks
the streets of this city.

291
00:23:39.419 --> 00:23:40.853
Back in the mud so soon?

292
00:23:45.858 --> 00:23:47.660
Yes, I see.

293
00:23:47.694 --> 00:23:50.496
Absolutely savage depiction
of me, I'm afraid.

294
00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.332
Got the hair
all wrong, and the nose, too.

295
00:23:52.365 --> 00:23:54.133
I'm new to this criminal life,

296
00:23:54.167 --> 00:23:56.536
but I never thought the authorities
would attack my vanity.

297
00:23:56.569 --> 00:23:59.472
They think I'm a murderer!

298
00:23:59.505 --> 00:24:01.608
I've been called
much worse things in my time.

299
00:24:04.911 --> 00:24:07.647
Besides... they're not
looking for you...

300
00:24:08.081 --> 00:24:09.515
...are they?

301
00:24:09.549 --> 00:24:11.884
They're looking for a piteous,
nameless hunchback.

302
00:24:11.918 --> 00:24:15.054
And Igor, I would like you
to look at yourself.

303
00:24:16.689 --> 00:24:19.659
Igor, that creature
no longer exists.

304
00:24:22.762 --> 00:24:23.762
Dinner.

305
00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:35.775
This is excellent.

306
00:24:37.577 --> 00:24:41.080
So... what brought you to
the circus in the first place?

307
00:24:41.814 --> 00:24:42.814
Cutlery.

308
00:24:44.117 --> 00:24:45.518
What?
Use it.

309
00:24:45.918 --> 00:24:46.918
Oh. Sorry.

310
00:24:47.220 --> 00:24:48.521
Wipe your hands.

311
00:24:51.057 --> 00:24:52.057
Animals.

312
00:24:53.626 --> 00:24:54.661
Parts.

313
00:24:56.696 --> 00:24:59.632
I am a student at
the Royal College of Medicine.

314
00:24:59.666 --> 00:25:01.267
The curriculum
is straightforward,

315
00:25:01.300 --> 00:25:03.503
the exams easy,
the professors...

316
00:25:03.536 --> 00:25:06.539
Oh! The professors are
men of limited ability

317
00:25:06.572 --> 00:25:08.174
and even more limited horizon.

318
00:25:08.207 --> 00:25:10.410
Why did you rescue me?

319
00:25:11.477 --> 00:25:13.913
You, my friend,
were an unexpected gift.

320
00:25:13.946 --> 00:25:15.948
It's not every day
I come across a man,

321
00:25:15.982 --> 00:25:18.685
albeit one suffering from
such grotesque deformity...

322
00:25:18.718 --> 00:25:23.222
...who is so clearly talented,
observant, and resourceful...

323
00:25:23.256 --> 00:25:27.694
...and in possession of the most
gifted pair of hands I have ever seen.

324
00:25:28.795 --> 00:25:30.830
My interest in you
does not stem from charity.

325
00:25:31.130 --> 00:25:32.999
Follow me.

326
00:25:33.032 --> 00:25:35.468
Before I met you,
I was to approach Mr. Barnaby

327
00:25:35.501 --> 00:25:37.770
about acquiring some of
your deceased animals.

328
00:25:37.804 --> 00:25:39.605
To what end? Study?

329
00:25:41.674 --> 00:25:44.677
No, not as you would
think of it.

330
00:25:44.711 --> 00:25:46.312
I am of the strong belief
that death

331
00:25:46.345 --> 00:25:48.481
can be made
a temporary condition.

332
00:25:48.514 --> 00:25:49.982
That's impossible.
Improbable, yes.

333
00:25:50.016 --> 00:25:51.016
Impossible, no.

334
00:25:51.451 --> 00:25:52.752
Life is temporary.

335
00:25:52.785 --> 00:25:54.921
Why should death
be any different?

336
00:25:54.954 --> 00:25:57.123
I have absolutely
no time for false modesty.

337
00:25:57.156 --> 00:25:58.758
So it is without pride
or shame

338
00:25:58.791 --> 00:26:00.351
that I declare my discovery
an act of...

339
00:26:00.793 --> 00:26:01.894
...genius.

340
00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:09.402
Those eyes...

341
00:26:09.435 --> 00:26:13.473
...they're over
three months old.

342
00:26:13.506 --> 00:26:15.942
And the liquid is an
electrically conductive jelly

343
00:26:15.975 --> 00:26:17.643
of my own device.

344
00:26:17.677 --> 00:26:20.046
Serves a double function:
To preserve and to...

345
00:26:21.047 --> 00:26:23.049
Well, just wait and see.

346
00:26:23.983 --> 00:26:26.886
It's all a matter
of conversion, you see?

347
00:26:26.919 --> 00:26:30.056
The conversion
of pure electrical energy

348
00:26:30.089 --> 00:26:31.824
into the biological variety...

349
00:26:31.858 --> 00:26:34.260
...that flows
through the human body.

350
00:26:34.293 --> 00:26:35.813
Hence, the construction
of this device:

351
00:26:36.229 --> 00:26:38.164
The Lazarus Fork.

352
00:26:38.197 --> 00:26:41.868
I have found that by passing
that current through a...

353
00:26:41.901 --> 00:26:44.804
...specially blended variety
of sulfates and metals...

354
00:26:44.837 --> 00:26:46.539
You've mastered
the conversion?

355
00:26:47.073 --> 00:26:48.073
Yes.

356
00:26:48.941 --> 00:26:50.042
Well, show me.

357
00:27:07.126 --> 00:27:08.126
Ready?

358
00:27:16.903 --> 00:27:18.938
There. Do you see?

359
00:27:20.339 --> 00:27:21.674
They live.

360
00:27:26.312 --> 00:27:27.713
What do you think?

361
00:27:29.315 --> 00:27:31.050
It is impressive.

362
00:27:31.083 --> 00:27:33.085
But you have
made a mess of the nerves.

363
00:27:35.922 --> 00:27:37.457
I beg your pardon?

364
00:27:37.490 --> 00:27:38.891
The oculomotor nerves.

365
00:27:38.925 --> 00:27:40.793
You haven't
connected them properly.

366
00:27:40.827 --> 00:27:42.829
That's why
they don't move evenly.

367
00:27:44.463 --> 00:27:45.698
You.

368
00:27:59.445 --> 00:28:01.013
There he is!

369
00:28:01.447 --> 00:28:03.216
That's the man.

370
00:28:03.249 --> 00:28:04.483
That's the man I'm after.

371
00:28:04.517 --> 00:28:05.685
Thank you for asking.

372
00:28:06.319 --> 00:28:07.787
You're welcome.

373
00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:10.556
Now, I shall bring you
your assignments piecemeal.

374
00:28:10.590 --> 00:28:12.058
You will complete them
in a timely fashion,

375
00:28:12.091 --> 00:28:15.328
whereon I shall apply them
to a larger...

376
00:28:15.361 --> 00:28:17.530
...whole of my own device.
Questions?

377
00:28:17.563 --> 00:28:19.398
Uh, this larger whole...

378
00:28:19.432 --> 00:28:21.567
...is not of your concern.

379
00:28:21.601 --> 00:28:22.568
Well, but if I...

380
00:28:22.602 --> 00:28:23.736
Igor, I...

381
00:28:30.676 --> 00:28:32.979
All this is now yours.

382
00:28:33.012 --> 00:28:35.381
Every book. Every piece
of reference material.

383
00:28:35.414 --> 00:28:36.414
Apparatus. Desk.

384
00:28:37.416 --> 00:28:39.318
Room. Your laboratory,
if you like.

385
00:28:45.791 --> 00:28:48.861
As my assistant, you shall be
at the very heart...

386
00:28:48.895 --> 00:28:52.198
...of a scientific enterprise
that will change the world.

387
00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:56.335
Now, will you help me?

388
00:29:12.585 --> 00:29:14.220
Yeah. Fix that.

389
00:29:14.253 --> 00:29:15.688
Ah. Thank you.

390
00:29:28.801 --> 00:29:30.102
Mmm-hmm.

391
00:29:40.413 --> 00:29:41.847
Keep working on it.

392
00:30:44.610 --> 00:30:46.730
<i>The hospital made
arrangements for Lorelei.</i>

393
00:30:47.380 --> 00:30:49.048
<i>She now had a benefactor.</i>

394
00:30:50.650 --> 00:30:52.118
<i>I was pleased
she had recovered</i>

395
00:30:52.151 --> 00:30:54.520
<i>and had someone
to look after her, but...</i>

396
00:30:54.553 --> 00:30:57.423
<i>...as the weeks went by,
I missed her.</i>

397
00:30:57.456 --> 00:31:00.059
<i>And I wondered if her life
had changed as much as mine.</i>

398
00:31:22.948 --> 00:31:23.949
Uh...

399
00:31:24.583 --> 00:31:25.918
Victor?
Mmm-hmm?

400
00:31:25.951 --> 00:31:27.853
This letter
for Master Straussman.

401
00:31:27.887 --> 00:31:30.356
We are going out on the town.
Oh!

402
00:31:32.358 --> 00:31:33.959
Here we are.

403
00:31:33.993 --> 00:31:35.661
I have a tenured membership
at the club,

404
00:31:35.694 --> 00:31:37.696
thanks to my father's...

405
00:31:37.730 --> 00:31:39.298
...status as a charter member.

406
00:31:39.331 --> 00:31:40.733
Bought the velvet
for the seats.

407
00:31:40.766 --> 00:31:42.001
Your father...

408
00:31:42.034 --> 00:31:43.769
Is what they call
a great man.

409
00:31:43.803 --> 00:31:46.672
Esteemed doctor,

410
00:31:46.705 --> 00:31:49.041
member of the Royal College
of Physicians, and...

411
00:31:49.075 --> 00:31:51.177
...pioneer in the field
of cardio-physiology.

412
00:31:51.210 --> 00:31:52.611
I should be honored
to meet him someday.

413
00:31:52.645 --> 00:31:54.847
Uh, perhaps not.
Look, here's the club!

414
00:31:54.880 --> 00:31:56.015
Master Victor, I'm not sure
I'm suited for this.

415
00:31:56.048 --> 00:31:57.383
Pish!

416
00:31:57.416 --> 00:31:59.218
Just keep your back straight,
your words clean,

417
00:31:59.251 --> 00:32:01.687
and do your damnedest
not to embarrass me.

418
00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:04.156
Babies grown in vats!

419
00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:06.158
Victor, do you think this is

420
00:32:06.192 --> 00:32:07.927
really the appropriate place
to talk about this?

421
00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:09.662
Help me!
I am just trying to inform

422
00:32:09.695 --> 00:32:12.364
these two wonderful
young ladies that...

423
00:32:12.398 --> 00:32:15.067
...fertilization needn't take
place inside the female body.

424
00:32:15.534 --> 00:32:17.236
Sperm! Sperms!

425
00:32:17.269 --> 00:32:18.971
Can sperm move?

426
00:32:19.004 --> 00:32:20.673
They can.
Thank you.

427
00:32:20.706 --> 00:32:22.608
Why can't
it move independently

428
00:32:22.641 --> 00:32:24.510
towards the egg in, say, a...

429
00:32:27.246 --> 00:32:28.781
...bucket?

430
00:32:28.814 --> 00:32:30.349
Where does the mother fit in?

431
00:32:31.617 --> 00:32:34.286
Exactly!
You're off educating yourself!

432
00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:36.989
By the time we need you,
we're...

433
00:32:37.022 --> 00:32:40.059
...sucking the fertilized egg
up into a funnel

434
00:32:40.092 --> 00:32:41.452
and then we shuck it
up your...

435
00:32:52.638 --> 00:32:54.039
Igor?

436
00:33:36.649 --> 00:33:37.917
Excuse me?

437
00:33:40.953 --> 00:33:42.454
Sorry, I thought
I recognized you.

438
00:33:42.488 --> 00:33:43.488
Well, you might do.

439
00:33:44.757 --> 00:33:46.358
I don't remember your name.

440
00:33:46.392 --> 00:33:48.561
Well, I never had one.

441
00:33:57.469 --> 00:33:58.504
It's you.

442
00:33:58.537 --> 00:33:59.537
It's me.

443
00:34:01.040 --> 00:34:02.608
Well, yeah, a bit different.

444
00:34:06.078 --> 00:34:07.613
You saved my life.

445
00:34:09.849 --> 00:34:11.317
My life.

446
00:34:16.689 --> 00:34:19.058
Boring!

447
00:34:19.091 --> 00:34:20.593
Friend of yours?

448
00:34:22.695 --> 00:34:23.996
That's Baron Bomine.

449
00:34:24.029 --> 00:34:26.599
He recruited me
to be in his cabaret...

450
00:34:26.632 --> 00:34:28.634
...and his consort in public.

451
00:34:29.969 --> 00:34:31.270
Right.

452
00:34:32.404 --> 00:34:35.341
He, uh... prefers
the company of men.

453
00:34:35.808 --> 00:34:36.942
Oh.

454
00:34:39.945 --> 00:34:42.348
I have a name now.

455
00:34:42.748 --> 00:34:44.216
I am Igor.

456
00:34:46.785 --> 00:34:47.785
What?

457
00:34:51.924 --> 00:34:53.459
It's perfect.

458
00:34:53.492 --> 00:34:55.094
This woman
seems to think

459
00:34:55.127 --> 00:34:56.895
that the human brain is pink.

460
00:34:56.929 --> 00:34:58.449
In fact, it is grey.

461
00:34:58.764 --> 00:35:00.566
That's Victor Frankenstein.

462
00:35:00.599 --> 00:35:02.468
- Grey like this oyster.
- I'm done.

463
00:35:02.501 --> 00:35:04.737
He's the man who rescued me.
And he helped save you.

464
00:35:04.770 --> 00:35:06.438
Is he always like that?

465
00:35:06.472 --> 00:35:09.875
No. He's very clever,
and he is kind.

466
00:35:09.909 --> 00:35:11.944
He just finds
ordinary people very...

467
00:35:11.977 --> 00:35:13.379
...ordinary.

468
00:35:13.913 --> 00:35:15.047
Victor, how did you...

469
00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:16.148
Who are you?

470
00:35:17.049 --> 00:35:20.719
You're the fallen angel.

471
00:35:20.753 --> 00:35:23.522
Plummeted from any other great
heights lately?

472
00:35:25.391 --> 00:35:27.860
Maybe you should try this one.
It's only, oh...

473
00:35:27.893 --> 00:35:29.962
...all of 30 feet.
You've had worse.

474
00:35:29.995 --> 00:35:31.597
I'm afraid the only thing
plummeting here

475
00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:33.766
is my opinion of you,
Mr. Frankenschteen.

476
00:35:33.799 --> 00:35:35.768
Frankenstein.
All right, Victor.

477
00:35:35.801 --> 00:35:38.037
Igor, um...

478
00:35:38.070 --> 00:35:39.938
Igor speaks
very highly of you.

479
00:35:39.972 --> 00:35:41.740
Would you like to join us?

480
00:35:43.275 --> 00:35:44.944
Now, of course,
I can't tell you everything,

481
00:35:44.977 --> 00:35:46.378
but suffice it to say...

482
00:35:46.412 --> 00:35:49.581
...Igor and I stand upon
the cusp of...

483
00:35:49.615 --> 00:35:53.485
...creating life out of death.

484
00:35:54.953 --> 00:35:57.056
Mr. Frankenstein...
Victor. Please.

485
00:35:57.089 --> 00:36:00.392
I find your promise
more than a little unsettling.

486
00:36:00.426 --> 00:36:01.927
Ooh.

487
00:36:01.960 --> 00:36:04.263
Superstitious, are we?
No.

488
00:36:04.296 --> 00:36:06.932
Are you not afraid to
challenge the natural order?

489
00:36:06.965 --> 00:36:08.600
Igor, speak up.
What do you think?

490
00:36:10.703 --> 00:36:12.638
Once, I would have agreed
with you, Lorelei,

491
00:36:12.671 --> 00:36:13.939
but think about it.

492
00:36:13.973 --> 00:36:15.341
Twenty years ago,
electric lights

493
00:36:15.374 --> 00:36:17.276
would have been
thought of as magic.

494
00:36:17.309 --> 00:36:20.245
Your injuries in the circus
would have been fatal.

495
00:36:20.279 --> 00:36:22.314
Every day science
and technology

496
00:36:22.348 --> 00:36:23.916
changes the way
we live our lives.

497
00:36:23.949 --> 00:36:25.284
Look at me.

498
00:36:25.317 --> 00:36:27.052
Well said, that man.

499
00:36:27.086 --> 00:36:28.087
Life and death are different.

500
00:36:28.120 --> 00:36:29.488
"Life and death!"

501
00:36:29.521 --> 00:36:32.758
I dream of a world
where hope replaces fear.

502
00:36:32.791 --> 00:36:34.660
A world where a murdered man

503
00:36:34.693 --> 00:36:36.428
can stand in court
to face his murderer.

504
00:36:36.462 --> 00:36:38.931
Where a crippled soldier,
shrapnel in his spine...

505
00:36:38.964 --> 00:36:40.933
...can be killed, healed,

506
00:36:40.966 --> 00:36:42.606
then brought back to life
to walk again.

507
00:36:43.902 --> 00:36:45.771
Don't you see?
The possibilities are...

508
00:36:46.939 --> 00:36:50.009
...endless! Life is beautiful!

509
00:36:50.042 --> 00:36:52.678
But unfortunately
it is finite.

510
00:36:52.711 --> 00:36:53.911
Now, tell me what that says.

511
00:36:54.913 --> 00:36:57.316
"Death."
Thank you very much.

512
00:36:57.349 --> 00:37:00.319
I cannot argue with that.

513
00:37:00.352 --> 00:37:03.122
There it is,
in black and white.

514
00:37:03.155 --> 00:37:05.557
But with a little
applied science...

515
00:37:08.260 --> 00:37:10.562
...what do I give you now?

516
00:37:10.596 --> 00:37:12.398
"Life."

517
00:37:13.232 --> 00:37:14.752
That's
what I'm trying to do.

518
00:37:15.801 --> 00:37:17.803
Perhaps I spoke too soon.

519
00:37:21.573 --> 00:37:23.333
<i>You shouldn't
see that girl again.</i>

520
00:37:23.409 --> 00:37:24.309
What? Why?

521
00:37:24.343 --> 00:37:25.778
Well, she's very nice.

522
00:37:25.811 --> 00:37:28.147
Uneducated, superstitious.
Distraction from our work.

523
00:37:28.180 --> 00:37:29.481
She's kind to me.

524
00:37:29.515 --> 00:37:31.350
Tonight was not about
meaningless frivolity.

525
00:37:31.383 --> 00:37:34.286
It was a celebration
of our work together.

526
00:37:34.319 --> 00:37:37.856
I think it is high time...
you met our monster.

527
00:37:44.897 --> 00:37:46.865
Don't tarry! Come, come, come!

528
00:37:49.001 --> 00:37:50.169
Come on!

529
00:38:33.011 --> 00:38:34.546
What is that?
Gordon.

530
00:38:35.981 --> 00:38:37.649
What?
Gordon!

531
00:38:40.185 --> 00:38:41.720
You made this?

532
00:38:41.753 --> 00:38:42.753
No, no, no.

533
00:38:43.689 --> 00:38:46.225
We... made this.

534
00:38:47.926 --> 00:38:50.696
Lungs, heart, spine, brain...

535
00:38:50.729 --> 00:38:51.897
...all your work.

536
00:38:54.600 --> 00:38:56.335
All...

537
00:38:56.368 --> 00:38:58.537
...impossible without you,
in fact.

538
00:39:00.506 --> 00:39:01.640
Victor...

539
00:39:05.377 --> 00:39:08.514
You promised me
this was all about life.

540
00:39:09.448 --> 00:39:11.250
It's about more than that.

541
00:39:18.724 --> 00:39:19.724
Hands off.

542
00:39:21.894 --> 00:39:23.328
Three... two...

543
00:39:24.096 --> 00:39:25.197
...one.

544
00:39:33.238 --> 00:39:34.758
Come on, come on, come on.

545
00:39:34.840 --> 00:39:36.275
Shh!

546
00:39:38.544 --> 00:39:39.578
Look.

547
00:39:52.624 --> 00:39:53.992
It's alive.

548
00:39:54.026 --> 00:39:57.596
Yes, it's... alive.

549
00:39:57.629 --> 00:39:58.864
It's alive?

550
00:39:59.932 --> 00:40:02.334
Victor... how?

551
00:40:02.367 --> 00:40:04.536
Can't quite move yet.

552
00:40:04.570 --> 00:40:06.338
Charge lasts barely an hour,

553
00:40:06.371 --> 00:40:07.839
and the bottom half

554
00:40:07.873 --> 00:40:09.608
is predominantly
a rude mockup.

555
00:40:09.641 --> 00:40:12.311
You have created life
out of nothing!

556
00:40:12.344 --> 00:40:14.446
Do you realize
how significant this is?

557
00:40:14.479 --> 00:40:15.981
Oh, I have an inkling.

558
00:40:17.416 --> 00:40:19.918
You are to accompany me
to the college tomorrow.

559
00:40:19.952 --> 00:40:21.954
I've announced that
I'll be making a presentation

560
00:40:21.987 --> 00:40:24.022
of my private work.

561
00:40:24.056 --> 00:40:25.791
I'm coming to the college
with you?

562
00:40:25.824 --> 00:40:27.025
As your assistant?

563
00:40:28.493 --> 00:40:30.729
Igor, try not to be
quite so dim.

564
00:40:31.496 --> 00:40:33.599
From this day forth...

565
00:40:33.632 --> 00:40:37.369
...you are to be my partner.

566
00:40:48.280 --> 00:40:49.881
Letter for you,
Miss Lorelei.

567
00:40:51.149 --> 00:40:53.018
Letter? From who?

568
00:41:01.893 --> 00:41:03.895
<i>Dear Lorelei:
We've had a breakthrough.</i>

569
00:41:03.929 --> 00:41:05.964
<i>Please come to
the Royal College of Medicine,</i>

570
00:41:05.998 --> 00:41:07.799
<i>Hall H, this evening at 8 PM.</i>

571
00:41:08.166 --> 00:41:09.166
<i>Igor.</i>

572
00:41:10.469 --> 00:41:12.371
Big presentation in Hall H.

573
00:41:13.538 --> 00:41:15.307
Presentation in Hall H.

574
00:41:16.275 --> 00:41:20.512
Big presentation, Hall H!

575
00:41:20.545 --> 00:41:21.980
Igor, around to the right.

576
00:41:29.554 --> 00:41:32.791
Since the beginning
of modern medicine...

577
00:41:32.824 --> 00:41:35.627
...there has been
an assumption...

578
00:41:35.661 --> 00:41:39.665
...regarding the status
of mortality...

579
00:41:39.698 --> 00:41:41.800
...that being that death...

580
00:41:41.833 --> 00:41:43.468
...is an unavoidable...

581
00:41:44.503 --> 00:41:48.540
...event, the inevitability of
which we should...

582
00:41:48.573 --> 00:41:50.542
...take for granted.

583
00:41:50.575 --> 00:41:52.077
I will show...

584
00:41:53.612 --> 00:41:56.882
...today
that life is not some...

585
00:41:58.383 --> 00:42:01.820
...grace bestowed
upon us by...

586
00:42:01.853 --> 00:42:03.755
...some outdated notion of
an all-powerful...

587
00:42:03.789 --> 00:42:06.992
Get on with it.

588
00:42:07.025 --> 00:42:10.095
Yes, of course. I'm not
accustomed to public speaking.

589
00:42:10.128 --> 00:42:12.698
Igor, would you prime
the dynamo for me, please?

590
00:42:12.731 --> 00:42:13.832
Yes, master.

591
00:42:15.133 --> 00:42:19.337
I would like to show you,
uh, show all seven of you...

592
00:42:19.371 --> 00:42:21.173
...and, of course,
the young lady...

593
00:42:21.206 --> 00:42:22.841
Come on, come on!

594
00:42:22.874 --> 00:42:23.909
I have a coach waiting.

595
00:42:25.410 --> 00:42:26.745
Uh...

596
00:42:28.146 --> 00:42:30.716
I give to you... life...

597
00:42:31.550 --> 00:42:34.386
...by my own... creation.

598
00:42:43.095 --> 00:42:44.463
Cattle market.

599
00:42:47.699 --> 00:42:52.037
I have built this homunculus
from various body parts...

600
00:42:52.070 --> 00:42:54.673
...I got from...
the London Zoo.

601
00:42:54.706 --> 00:42:56.141
They've had a terrible time
with the upkeep

602
00:42:56.174 --> 00:42:57.476
of their exotic animals,

603
00:42:57.509 --> 00:42:58.744
all to my benefit.

604
00:42:58.777 --> 00:43:00.712
He's mainly chimpanzee...

605
00:43:00.746 --> 00:43:02.314
...but with the aid of
my esteemed associate,

606
00:43:02.347 --> 00:43:03.582
Igor Straussman,

607
00:43:03.615 --> 00:43:05.016
we've managed to interlace...

608
00:43:05.050 --> 00:43:06.585
...multiple individuals,

609
00:43:06.618 --> 00:43:09.688
multiple species
as a matter of fact.

610
00:43:09.721 --> 00:43:11.823
Igor, is it ready?
They're staring at me.

611
00:43:11.857 --> 00:43:13.258
Thank you.

612
00:43:13.291 --> 00:43:15.160
Do come to the front.
Get a closer look.

613
00:43:15.193 --> 00:43:16.193
Don't be shy.

614
00:43:18.263 --> 00:43:20.165
He won't bite.

615
00:43:20.198 --> 00:43:23.835
Now, by the miracle
of electricity...

616
00:43:24.603 --> 00:43:28.774
...I give you in three,
two, one...

617
00:43:29.708 --> 00:43:31.109
...life.

618
00:43:37.015 --> 00:43:38.316
God!

619
00:43:38.350 --> 00:43:40.185
I've seen enough.

620
00:43:40.218 --> 00:43:41.453
No!

621
00:43:42.154 --> 00:43:43.722
Don't go!

622
00:43:43.755 --> 00:43:45.924
Igor, shock him again. Harder.

623
00:43:48.093 --> 00:43:50.328
Three, two, one... now!

624
00:43:53.799 --> 00:43:56.201
Frankenstein, you've surpassed...

625
00:43:56.234 --> 00:43:58.303
...all expectations, even by

626
00:43:58.336 --> 00:44:01.440
your own expansive mythos of
strangeness and perversion.

627
00:44:01.473 --> 00:44:03.475
This is spectacular.
It's delightful!

628
00:44:04.142 --> 00:44:06.311
Just an exquisite show of...

629
00:44:06.344 --> 00:44:07.612
...depraved lunacy.

630
00:44:07.913 --> 00:44:08.914
Igor.

631
00:44:09.581 --> 00:44:11.016
Full charge.

632
00:44:11.383 --> 00:44:12.751
Ready?

633
00:44:16.221 --> 00:44:17.989
Igor?
Ready.

634
00:44:18.456 --> 00:44:19.558
Now!

635
00:44:24.696 --> 00:44:26.998
Oh, look,
there she goes, Victor.

636
00:44:27.032 --> 00:44:29.167
Bing, bang... boom.

637
00:44:30.402 --> 00:44:31.770
What have you got next?

638
00:44:33.004 --> 00:44:34.706
Perhaps a midget

639
00:44:34.739 --> 00:44:36.808
hidden inside your rotting
meat sculpture's stomach...

640
00:44:36.842 --> 00:44:38.910
...ready to pop out
with a bouquet of ro...

641
00:45:03.268 --> 00:45:04.536
Do you see?

642
00:45:35.233 --> 00:45:36.233
It's all right.

643
00:45:37.035 --> 00:45:38.570
Gordon... Gordon...

644
00:45:39.404 --> 00:45:41.172
Igor!
Lorelei, stay back!

645
00:45:59.291 --> 00:46:01.293
Lorelei, are you all right?
Igor!

646
00:46:01.326 --> 00:46:02.661
I'm fine.

647
00:46:02.694 --> 00:46:04.596
Don't let him escape.

648
00:47:23.041 --> 00:47:24.275
Gordon! Stop!

649
00:47:25.377 --> 00:47:26.544
Ahh!

650
00:47:39.457 --> 00:47:41.459
No, no! Don't go out there!

651
00:48:09.154 --> 00:48:10.655
Victor!

652
00:48:10.688 --> 00:48:12.390
Calm down, Gordon.
Get him off me!

653
00:48:12.424 --> 00:48:13.658
Gordon?

654
00:48:13.692 --> 00:48:14.826
Victor!

655
00:48:16.694 --> 00:48:17.796
Ahh!

656
00:48:19.130 --> 00:48:21.332
Igor,
what have you done to him?

657
00:48:21.366 --> 00:48:22.446
Victor! Help me, not him!

658
00:48:28.540 --> 00:48:29.974
Victor, we have to kill it!

659
00:48:35.647 --> 00:48:37.182
Do it, Victor!

660
00:48:41.553 --> 00:48:42.854
<i>It was out of control!</i>

661
00:48:42.887 --> 00:48:44.923
We made progress today!

662
00:48:44.956 --> 00:48:46.958
It was homicidal!

663
00:48:46.991 --> 00:48:49.060
I had no way of knowing
that Gordon...

664
00:48:49.094 --> 00:48:50.774
Am I to understand
that you built that?

665
00:48:51.062 --> 00:48:52.363
Yes!

666
00:48:58.136 --> 00:48:59.237
I apologize.

667
00:49:00.338 --> 00:49:02.841
I misjudged you.

668
00:49:03.541 --> 00:49:04.843
Your flaws, though they're...

669
00:49:05.844 --> 00:49:08.179
...glaring and massive,
are merely social...

670
00:49:08.746 --> 00:49:09.981
...not intellectual.

671
00:49:11.649 --> 00:49:13.118
I find your work
astonishing...

672
00:49:14.252 --> 00:49:15.987
...and to be
perfectly frank...

673
00:49:16.888 --> 00:49:19.824
...brilliant. Brilliant!

674
00:49:19.858 --> 00:49:22.861
Quite beyond
my own ability to comprehend.

675
00:49:25.697 --> 00:49:26.931
Could you create another one?

676
00:49:26.965 --> 00:49:29.968
I could,
and a whole lot more beside.

677
00:49:31.703 --> 00:49:34.973
But that would take
considerable resource.

678
00:49:35.006 --> 00:49:36.474
As you are aware,

679
00:49:36.508 --> 00:49:38.676
I do come from the third
richest family in England.

680
00:49:38.710 --> 00:49:40.678
As a result, I can provide you

681
00:49:40.712 --> 00:49:42.152
with whatever it is
you so require.

682
00:49:42.614 --> 00:49:44.916
In that case, yes.

683
00:49:44.949 --> 00:49:47.418
And when you say... "more"?

684
00:49:47.819 --> 00:49:49.020
A man.

685
00:49:51.089 --> 00:49:53.758
A thinking, intelligent being.

686
00:49:53.791 --> 00:49:54.893
Can we discuss this?

687
00:49:54.926 --> 00:49:56.294
I like this ambition.

688
00:49:56.327 --> 00:49:58.930
You were right, Igor.
The beast was dangerous...

689
00:49:58.963 --> 00:50:00.532
...but now we have
the opportunity

690
00:50:00.565 --> 00:50:02.300
to show the value of our work.

691
00:50:02.333 --> 00:50:06.304
You and I, Igor... we shall
create a man after our own...

692
00:50:06.738 --> 00:50:08.039
...image.

693
00:50:09.474 --> 00:50:10.909
Think of it.

694
00:50:12.677 --> 00:50:13.677
An intelligent...

695
00:50:14.379 --> 00:50:16.047
...civilized...

696
00:50:17.448 --> 00:50:18.917
...man.

697
00:50:22.687 --> 00:50:24.322
I'll want
another demonstration.

698
00:50:25.456 --> 00:50:27.525
I want to know whether you can
take direction.

699
00:50:27.559 --> 00:50:28.760
Follow orders, so to speak.

700
00:50:28.793 --> 00:50:30.495
Is that a problem?

701
00:50:30.528 --> 00:50:32.564
Victor, we cannot.
No.

702
00:50:32.597 --> 00:50:33.898
Excellent!

703
00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:37.569
Expect to hear from me soon.

704
00:50:41.773 --> 00:50:44.175
You did not create
this technology

705
00:50:44.209 --> 00:50:45.710
and yet you presume to
tell me how to use it.

706
00:50:45.743 --> 00:50:47.212
You should know your place!

707
00:50:50.081 --> 00:50:52.550
Your ignorance
of the ways of the world

708
00:50:52.584 --> 00:50:54.552
cannot hinder the furtherment
of my experimentation.

709
00:50:54.586 --> 00:50:56.621
But surely you see
you have no control.

710
00:50:56.654 --> 00:50:58.590
Surely you have forgotten

711
00:50:58.623 --> 00:51:00.358
what I did for you
at the circus!

712
00:51:02.427 --> 00:51:06.297
This is my destiny.
It is your destiny.

713
00:51:06.331 --> 00:51:10.568
And that man represents
our only ally on this planet.

714
00:51:10.602 --> 00:51:13.705
And if he wants us to make him
an entire zoo of homunculi,

715
00:51:13.738 --> 00:51:15.573
that is exactly
what we will do...

716
00:51:15.607 --> 00:51:17.976
...if it ensures the
furtherment of our research.

717
00:51:18.009 --> 00:51:20.111
Am I making myself clear?

718
00:51:20.712 --> 00:51:22.380
Am I making myself clear?!

719
00:51:22.413 --> 00:51:23.514
Yes, Victor!

720
00:52:04.889 --> 00:52:06.424
<i>I own you!</i>

721
00:52:07.759 --> 00:52:08.839
<i>You belong to the circus!</i>

722
00:52:19.604 --> 00:52:22.073
Good morning. Can I help you?

723
00:52:22.106 --> 00:52:24.575
Detective Inspector Turpin,
Scotland Yard.

724
00:52:26.511 --> 00:52:28.579
I want to speak with
a Mr. Frankenstein.

725
00:52:30.081 --> 00:52:31.649
I'm afraid
that's not convenient

726
00:52:31.683 --> 00:52:32.951
at the moment, sir.

727
00:52:32.984 --> 00:52:34.986
May I know your business?

728
00:52:58.076 --> 00:52:59.544
Do you miss the circus?

729
00:53:01.879 --> 00:53:03.414
I'm not sure
what you mean, sir.

730
00:53:04.582 --> 00:53:06.084
Get me Frankenstein.

731
00:53:28.206 --> 00:53:30.708
I've informed the college
I would happily pay

732
00:53:30.742 --> 00:53:32.310
for the damage.
Just a bit of broken glass.

733
00:53:32.343 --> 00:53:34.078
An animal
was involved apparently.

734
00:53:34.112 --> 00:53:35.913
There was indeed.

735
00:53:35.947 --> 00:53:38.783
Mr. Straussman and I are currently
involved in the study of...

736
00:53:39.417 --> 00:53:41.185
...chimpanzees.

737
00:53:41.219 --> 00:53:45.223
It's quite... quite
fascinating, actually.

738
00:53:45.256 --> 00:53:47.792
We have discovered that
by using emotional cues...

739
00:53:47.825 --> 00:53:50.495
...we can teach them
primitive belief systems.

740
00:53:50.528 --> 00:53:52.163
Of course, it's only because
they are not yet capable

741
00:53:52.196 --> 00:53:54.399
of higher logical thought.

742
00:53:55.666 --> 00:53:56.601
Where is the creature now?

743
00:53:56.634 --> 00:53:58.169
Dead.

744
00:53:58.202 --> 00:54:00.505
Poor thing.
Had to be put down, didn't it?

745
00:54:00.538 --> 00:54:03.040
Why would the police be
interested in such a trifle?

746
00:54:03.074 --> 00:54:04.409
There may be a connection

747
00:54:04.442 --> 00:54:05.922
with a murder investigation
of ours.

748
00:54:06.778 --> 00:54:08.212
Murder investigation?

749
00:54:08.246 --> 00:54:10.181
Igor, this is
a murder investigation!

750
00:54:10.214 --> 00:54:11.482
Am I to understand
we have to summon

751
00:54:11.516 --> 00:54:13.618
the chimpanzee's lawyer?

752
00:54:15.853 --> 00:54:17.422
Mr. Frankenstein, I warn you

753
00:54:17.455 --> 00:54:20.725
that there are consequences
for obstructing police work.

754
00:54:20.758 --> 00:54:22.860
I should like to see records
of your experiments

755
00:54:22.894 --> 00:54:24.495
for the past twelve months.

756
00:54:24.529 --> 00:54:26.631
If you cannot cooperate,
then, by God,

757
00:54:26.664 --> 00:54:29.100
I'll conduct a thorough search
of these premises.

758
00:54:29.133 --> 00:54:30.535
"By God," you say?

759
00:54:34.138 --> 00:54:35.706
Inspector,
I must inform you...

760
00:54:35.740 --> 00:54:37.308
...that you are currently
in the home of rational,

761
00:54:37.341 --> 00:54:38.943
free-thinking men.

762
00:54:38.976 --> 00:54:40.578
To violate it or my research

763
00:54:40.611 --> 00:54:42.113
would require
a proper legal warrant.

764
00:54:42.146 --> 00:54:43.748
And God has no authority here.

765
00:54:43.781 --> 00:54:45.183
Tread lightly, sir.

766
00:54:46.150 --> 00:54:47.385
You may insult me,

767
00:54:47.418 --> 00:54:50.321
but you impugn the Lord
at your peril.

768
00:54:50.354 --> 00:54:52.723
I should remind you that life
is a sacred creation.

769
00:54:54.292 --> 00:54:56.928
Are you a police officer
or a theologian?

770
00:54:56.961 --> 00:54:58.162
Let me tell you something
for nothing.

771
00:54:58.196 --> 00:55:01.365
Life... I'll say this
very slowly... is merely...

772
00:55:01.399 --> 00:55:04.168
...the application and outcome
of applied chemistry.

773
00:55:04.202 --> 00:55:06.137
And did you or did you not
apply such chemistry

774
00:55:06.170 --> 00:55:07.939
at the Royal College
of Medicine two days ago?

775
00:55:07.972 --> 00:55:10.641
Igor, when was the last time
you went to confession?

776
00:55:10.675 --> 00:55:13.444
The good friar has come to see
whether we have sinned.

777
00:55:13.478 --> 00:55:15.079
"He that covereth his sin
shall not prosper."

778
00:55:15.112 --> 00:55:16.147
I'll ask you again.

779
00:55:16.180 --> 00:55:17.915
And I will ask you again, sir:

780
00:55:17.949 --> 00:55:19.283
Why are you so interested,

781
00:55:19.317 --> 00:55:21.118
nay, infatuated
with this case?

782
00:55:21.152 --> 00:55:22.787
Surely there are
more interesting mysteries

783
00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:24.222
to be solved in London.

784
00:55:24.856 --> 00:55:26.424
Or...

785
00:55:26.457 --> 00:55:28.392
...is it precisely
because this experiment,

786
00:55:28.426 --> 00:55:30.828
which you imagine
took place...

787
00:55:30.862 --> 00:55:32.363
...may very well discredit

788
00:55:32.396 --> 00:55:34.165
your own primitive
belief system?

789
00:55:34.198 --> 00:55:36.400
Uncover what you will
about me, Inspector.

790
00:55:36.434 --> 00:55:38.336
Men like you have always stood
in the way of progress

791
00:55:38.369 --> 00:55:41.072
and invariably been
left in its wake.

792
00:55:41.105 --> 00:55:42.640
My creation...!

793
00:55:51.215 --> 00:55:53.484
Be careful, Mr. Frankenstein.

794
00:55:54.252 --> 00:55:56.521
You toy with wrathful forces.

795
00:55:58.456 --> 00:56:00.625
And there's no mercy
in nature.

796
00:56:06.097 --> 00:56:07.365
Good day.

797
00:56:11.402 --> 00:56:12.937
I'll be back with a warrant.

798
00:56:32.056 --> 00:56:34.425
That thing
in the school, Igor...

799
00:56:36.661 --> 00:56:38.942
...I looked into its eyes
and there was nothing there.

800
00:56:43.868 --> 00:56:46.070
There is a difference
between using your machines...

801
00:56:46.103 --> 00:56:48.906
...to restore a life
wrongly lost and...

802
00:56:48.940 --> 00:56:51.442
...to create something that
was never supposed to exist.

803
00:56:52.543 --> 00:56:53.978
Victor must understand that.

804
00:56:54.512 --> 00:56:55.512
Look...

805
00:56:56.681 --> 00:56:59.617
...I never thought
I'd leave the circus.

806
00:56:59.650 --> 00:57:02.820
I thought I'd be in there
till I died. And Victor...

807
00:57:02.853 --> 00:57:05.289
...has given me all this.

808
00:57:06.557 --> 00:57:09.327
And all he asked
is that I believe in him.

809
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:11.362
I understand that, Igor.

810
00:57:11.395 --> 00:57:13.664
What I'm saying is...

811
00:57:13.698 --> 00:57:16.334
...don't let yourself be
bullied by anyone ever again.

812
00:57:18.169 --> 00:57:19.704
Victor says he's your friend.

813
00:57:20.972 --> 00:57:23.040
But if you believe
Victor is on a wrong path,

814
00:57:23.074 --> 00:57:24.709
then you must make a stand.

815
00:57:31.782 --> 00:57:33.351
I have to go.

816
00:57:42.660 --> 00:57:46.664
Victor, if you truly respect
me as a scientist...

817
00:57:46.697 --> 00:57:48.766
If you truly respect me
as your friend...

818
00:57:49.634 --> 00:57:51.602
...you must listen
to my concerns.

819
00:57:56.574 --> 00:57:57.908
Igor.

820
00:57:57.942 --> 00:57:59.610
Sir.

821
00:57:59.644 --> 00:58:01.512
What's it been? Three years?

822
00:58:02.413 --> 00:58:03.781
You look slimmer.

823
00:58:04.915 --> 00:58:07.318
I'm sorry, sir, I don't...

824
00:58:07.351 --> 00:58:09.120
Is Victor here?
Yes, sir.

825
00:58:09.153 --> 00:58:10.488
Very well.

826
00:58:13.290 --> 00:58:15.092
Where have you been?

827
00:58:15.126 --> 00:58:17.762
Not wise to be out on the town
when there's a manhunt on.

828
00:58:18.496 --> 00:58:20.531
Get off his heart!

829
00:58:23.834 --> 00:58:24.834
Father.

830
00:58:25.603 --> 00:58:26.637
Get up.

831
00:58:29.073 --> 00:58:30.408
Leave.

832
00:58:34.111 --> 00:58:36.147
Father, I'm so excited
that you've come.

833
00:58:36.180 --> 00:58:37.415
Your timing is impeccable.

834
00:58:37.448 --> 00:58:38.349
I've had such
breakthroughs with my...

835
00:58:38.382 --> 00:58:39.684
I don't care.

836
00:58:41.085 --> 00:58:43.721
I don't care about your poorly
researched theories

837
00:58:43.754 --> 00:58:45.456
or your disastrous experiments.

838
00:58:45.489 --> 00:58:46.924
Not poorly researched,
I've told you...

839
00:58:46.957 --> 00:58:48.659
Victor, silence.

840
00:58:49.727 --> 00:58:51.862
Yesterday I received
a telegram...

841
00:58:51.896 --> 00:58:53.597
...informing me
that you are to go

842
00:58:53.631 --> 00:58:55.733
before the board of directors
at the college.

843
00:58:55.766 --> 00:58:57.902
They say you neglect
your schoolwork.

844
00:59:01.672 --> 00:59:03.574
They intend to expel you.

845
00:59:07.411 --> 00:59:09.447
No, they can't!

846
00:59:09.847 --> 00:59:11.115
Can't they?

847
00:59:11.148 --> 00:59:12.717
The work I am doing
is far more important...

848
00:59:12.750 --> 00:59:14.018
...than anything
they are conducting

849
00:59:14.051 --> 00:59:15.986
at that damn school.
You're a fool, Victor.

850
00:59:16.020 --> 00:59:17.822
You always have been.

851
00:59:19.490 --> 00:59:21.425
If only you could have been
more like Henry.

852
00:59:22.126 --> 00:59:23.561
But you...

853
00:59:25.129 --> 00:59:27.932
You just bring shame
to the name Frankenstein.

854
00:59:27.965 --> 00:59:29.500
I will ensure
that the name of Frankenstein

855
00:59:29.533 --> 00:59:30.601
is never forgotten!

856
00:59:35.139 --> 00:59:36.874
You've done it again, Victor.

857
00:59:38.676 --> 00:59:41.445
Only this time it's your own
life you've ruined.

858
01:00:24.989 --> 01:00:26.757
So, what's this, then?

859
01:00:27.258 --> 01:00:29.059
Finnegan's project.

860
01:00:30.461 --> 01:00:31.662
My man.

861
01:00:33.764 --> 01:00:36.167
He was going to be
the modern Prometheus.

862
01:00:38.169 --> 01:00:40.771
Stupid, stupid, stupid.

863
01:00:44.341 --> 01:00:46.043
He's also not nearly
big enough.

864
01:00:46.610 --> 01:00:48.045
Yes. What?

865
01:00:49.313 --> 01:00:51.649
Gordon was fast
and strong, sure,

866
01:00:51.682 --> 01:00:52.983
but he couldn't sustain
any of that.

867
01:00:53.017 --> 01:00:54.051
And towards the end,

868
01:00:54.084 --> 01:00:55.920
he was having some
real trouble breathing.

869
01:00:55.953 --> 01:00:57.822
Breathing?

870
01:00:57.855 --> 01:01:00.691
Embolisms. Embolisms
in his lungs. Yes, of course.

871
01:01:01.525 --> 01:01:03.961
How stupid.

872
01:01:03.994 --> 01:01:06.363
So much raw energy
coursing around his structure.

873
01:01:06.397 --> 01:01:08.065
His body couldn't
take the charge.

874
01:01:08.098 --> 01:01:10.501
Wretched creature would have
been dead in ten minutes.

875
01:01:10.534 --> 01:01:13.270
If we want to build something
that can live and stay alive,

876
01:01:13.304 --> 01:01:14.605
we'll need a lot more energy.

877
01:01:14.638 --> 01:01:16.173
Tons more.

878
01:01:16.207 --> 01:01:18.576
Just stop. What could possibly
generate that kind of...?

879
01:01:19.643 --> 01:01:20.945
Lightning!

880
01:01:23.514 --> 01:01:25.249
Yes, I have...

881
01:01:25.282 --> 01:01:26.684
...just the thing.

882
01:01:26.717 --> 01:01:29.119
One of my early designs
for the Lazarus Fork...

883
01:01:29.153 --> 01:01:30.454
...incorporated a structure

884
01:01:30.487 --> 01:01:33.324
that actually
sucked its energy...

885
01:01:33.357 --> 01:01:35.659
...from the atmosphere.

886
01:01:35.693 --> 01:01:37.761
It's possible that we can
build a larger version

887
01:01:37.795 --> 01:01:38.963
that would simulate
a static burst...

888
01:01:38.996 --> 01:01:41.599
...similar to
that of lightning.

889
01:01:41.632 --> 01:01:43.834
No, it's the same problem.

890
01:01:43.868 --> 01:01:46.871
We can't just make the body
accept that charge.

891
01:01:46.904 --> 01:01:49.807
We are incapable of simply
making larger organs.

892
01:01:49.840 --> 01:01:51.320
What if we gave him
two sets of lungs?

893
01:01:57.882 --> 01:01:59.402
You know you're brilliant,
don't you?

894
01:02:00.784 --> 01:02:03.821
Why wouldn't we? He's our man.
We can do what we like.

895
01:02:03.854 --> 01:02:06.090
Not just two sets of lungs...

896
01:02:06.123 --> 01:02:07.725
Two hearts.
Yes!

897
01:02:07.758 --> 01:02:09.493
Pump all that blood
around the larger body.

898
01:02:09.526 --> 01:02:11.046
Absolutely. He'd need it.

899
01:02:13.397 --> 01:02:15.466
Igor...

900
01:02:15.499 --> 01:02:17.234
Earlier, when my father
was here...

901
01:02:17.268 --> 01:02:19.103
I was reading.

902
01:02:19.136 --> 01:02:20.404
I didn't hear a thing.

903
01:02:20.437 --> 01:02:21.757
Did he say
anything interesting?

904
01:02:26.210 --> 01:02:27.311
No, he didn't.

905
01:02:27.878 --> 01:02:28.878
Whiskey?

906
01:02:29.480 --> 01:02:31.315
Yes. Yes, do that.

907
01:02:40.558 --> 01:02:42.459
A larger chest cavity...

908
01:02:42.493 --> 01:02:44.828
...to incorporate four lungs.

909
01:02:44.862 --> 01:02:46.302
Two sets on the left
and the right.

910
01:02:49.366 --> 01:02:51.602
Bigger with the arms! Biceps.

911
01:02:52.803 --> 01:02:54.738
Now what do we do?
Tilt him.

912
01:02:54.772 --> 01:02:56.073
Backwards and forwards.

913
01:02:56.106 --> 01:02:57.775
Let that liquid
run through the body.

914
01:02:59.910 --> 01:03:01.478
Cheers.
Here's to him.

915
01:03:01.512 --> 01:03:02.813
Flat head.

916
01:03:04.281 --> 01:03:05.716
Why?

917
01:03:05.749 --> 01:03:08.085
Because I like it, that's why.

918
01:03:11.889 --> 01:03:13.490
To his two hearts.

919
01:03:25.336 --> 01:03:26.370
Mmm...

920
01:03:37.281 --> 01:03:38.649
Is that precious?

921
01:03:45.489 --> 01:03:47.569
They've denied us
the warrant, Inspector.

922
01:03:49.493 --> 01:03:51.228
As the Magistrate said,

923
01:03:51.261 --> 01:03:53.297
with no sign of any foul play,
nor indeed of any crime...

924
01:03:53.330 --> 01:03:54.698
No foul play?

925
01:03:55.699 --> 01:03:57.735
Look at the debris
at the Royal College.

926
01:03:57.768 --> 01:03:59.203
Acid burns, the same.

927
01:03:59.236 --> 01:04:00.738
Bloody paw prints
on the floor.

928
01:04:00.771 --> 01:04:02.139
Something's going on.

929
01:04:02.172 --> 01:04:04.212
Something's happening
in that basement, I know it.

930
01:04:04.274 --> 01:04:06.076
I know it.

931
01:04:06.110 --> 01:04:09.013
And it's my job, my duty.
It's my moral duty to stop it.

932
01:04:09.980 --> 01:04:12.516
But, sir, you have no warrant.

933
01:04:12.549 --> 01:04:14.084
Yes, he's insulted you.

934
01:04:14.118 --> 01:04:15.285
Yes, he's clever.
But we have no evidence.

935
01:04:15.719 --> 01:04:16.887
I don't care.

936
01:04:20.024 --> 01:04:21.864
I need to find out
what's in that basement.

937
01:04:23.093 --> 01:04:25.029
Now we can enact
my true vision.

938
01:04:25.062 --> 01:04:26.964
You and I will take
life's raw elements,

939
01:04:26.997 --> 01:04:30.234
its base components, and we...

940
01:04:30.267 --> 01:04:32.202
...shall assemble them
to our own specification,

941
01:04:32.236 --> 01:04:33.236
to our own design.

942
01:04:34.838 --> 01:04:37.474
For tonight we begin
our model...

943
01:04:38.142 --> 01:04:39.476
...of Prometheus.

944
01:04:41.311 --> 01:04:42.346
Um...

945
01:04:44.214 --> 01:04:47.751
Tonight... actually, Victor,
I was...

946
01:04:47.785 --> 01:04:48.652
I've been invited to a ball.

947
01:04:48.685 --> 01:04:50.287
A what?

948
01:04:50.320 --> 01:04:51.422
A ball. Lorelei's asked me.

949
01:04:51.455 --> 01:04:52.489
Lorelei?

950
01:04:53.524 --> 01:04:56.193
Yes.
No, no, don't speak.

951
01:04:57.094 --> 01:04:58.095
Lorelei...

952
01:04:59.930 --> 01:05:01.498
I shall stay here and work.

953
01:05:02.633 --> 01:05:04.368
I'm sorry, Victor.
No need to apologize.

954
01:05:06.003 --> 01:05:08.505
You should go off and enjoy
yourself. You deserve it.

955
01:05:09.173 --> 01:05:10.240
You've earned it.

956
01:05:11.408 --> 01:05:12.476
You can go now.

957
01:05:13.777 --> 01:05:14.845
Thank you.

958
01:06:26.450 --> 01:06:28.051
I don't know what to do.

959
01:06:30.120 --> 01:06:31.922
You're already doing it.

960
01:06:56.146 --> 01:06:58.182
Frankenstein,
open this door!

961
01:06:59.416 --> 01:07:00.884
We'll break it down!

962
01:07:00.918 --> 01:07:03.353
Open this door now!
Scotland Yard!

963
01:07:07.057 --> 01:07:09.493
Frankenstein! Open the door!

964
01:07:14.231 --> 01:07:17.601
One, two, three.
One, two, three.

965
01:07:17.868 --> 01:07:19.336
Harder.

966
01:07:25.209 --> 01:07:28.078
Frankenstein! Open the door!

967
01:07:30.681 --> 01:07:32.382
Victor, we have to leave!

968
01:07:32.416 --> 01:07:34.851
Where have you been?
With Lorelei.

969
01:07:34.885 --> 01:07:37.521
Oh, I see.
Wasting your time...

970
01:07:37.554 --> 01:07:39.690
...with pointless courtship...

971
01:07:39.723 --> 01:07:42.726
...while it remains to me to
take care of the work in hand!

972
01:07:42.759 --> 01:07:44.995
Frankenstein!
Open this door!

973
01:07:46.263 --> 01:07:49.766
Frankenstein, we're coming in!
Get this door down.

974
01:07:49.800 --> 01:07:50.834
I've sent for
one of Finnegan's men

975
01:07:50.867 --> 01:07:52.102
to provide a carriage.

976
01:07:52.135 --> 01:07:53.971
I'm trying to
overload the conductors.

977
01:07:54.004 --> 01:07:56.273
Forget the conductors!
We have to get out of here!

978
01:07:56.306 --> 01:07:59.376
And let them have my machines?
Not bloody likely!

979
01:08:01.245 --> 01:08:02.946
Trap door to the sewers...
it's the only way out.

980
01:08:02.980 --> 01:08:04.114
Try and open it.

981
01:08:10.087 --> 01:08:12.289
Pickaxe on the ice closet.

982
01:08:18.562 --> 01:08:20.397
What are you waiting for?
What is that?!

983
01:08:20.430 --> 01:08:22.165
Oh. Uh...

984
01:08:22.199 --> 01:08:24.167
Igor Straussman,
meet Igor Straussman.

985
01:08:25.269 --> 01:08:28.338
What? What did you do to him?!

986
01:08:28.372 --> 01:08:30.741
Found him like that
a couple months ago. Overdose.

987
01:08:30.774 --> 01:08:33.911
A couple of months?
You took his eyes!

988
01:08:33.944 --> 01:08:35.212
Victor, what is
wrong with you?

989
01:08:35.245 --> 01:08:36.813
You want to die in prison...

990
01:08:36.847 --> 01:08:38.815
...executed by that maniac?

991
01:08:38.849 --> 01:08:40.183
Hunchback!

992
01:08:42.586 --> 01:08:44.054
Do you see the truth now?

993
01:08:45.155 --> 01:08:47.925
This is the man
who took you from the circus.

994
01:08:47.958 --> 01:08:50.127
Who would gouge the eyes
from a dead friend.

995
01:08:50.160 --> 01:08:51.600
Move once more
and I'll kill you.

996
01:08:53.230 --> 01:08:56.066
Do as you wish.
I have no fear of death!

997
01:08:56.767 --> 01:08:57.767
Really?

998
01:08:59.303 --> 01:09:00.304
I do.

999
01:09:02.072 --> 01:09:03.473
I lost my wife...

1000
01:09:05.542 --> 01:09:07.044
...to a malign growth.

1001
01:09:08.445 --> 01:09:10.480
And in my suffering
I know about death.

1002
01:09:11.615 --> 01:09:13.450
That it's an abyss from which

1003
01:09:13.483 --> 01:09:16.320
no man nor woman
can be returned.

1004
01:09:18.021 --> 01:09:20.490
Would you not rather
have her by your side?

1005
01:09:20.524 --> 01:09:22.326
Would you not have her
live again?

1006
01:09:23.927 --> 01:09:25.362
She is alive.

1007
01:09:26.797 --> 01:09:28.065
In God's house.

1008
01:09:28.999 --> 01:09:30.600
And when I, too,
fall into that abyss...

1009
01:09:31.868 --> 01:09:33.337
...I shall be by her side.

1010
01:09:34.404 --> 01:09:37.641
Don't you see?
You trust in a fiction!

1011
01:09:38.642 --> 01:09:40.210
And you shall be forgotten.

1012
01:09:41.645 --> 01:09:42.645
That's right.

1013
01:09:43.880 --> 01:09:46.249
History will bury you,
Frankenstein...

1014
01:09:46.283 --> 01:09:48.151
...and no man
will remember your name.

1015
01:09:48.185 --> 01:09:49.753
No, you're wrong. Igor, no!

1016
01:09:54.858 --> 01:09:56.360
You'll remember me now.

1017
01:10:11.608 --> 01:10:12.608
Victor!

1018
01:10:20.784 --> 01:10:22.152
Come on, Igor!

1019
01:10:25.889 --> 01:10:27.157
Pull! Pull!

1020
01:10:34.698 --> 01:10:36.800
Frankenstein, we're coming in!

1021
01:10:38.468 --> 01:10:39.603
Inspector?

1022
01:10:47.844 --> 01:10:49.312
Finnegan.

1023
01:10:50.180 --> 01:10:52.549
Finnegan! Where are you?

1024
01:10:52.582 --> 01:10:56.453
Frankenstein! Igor!
What an unexpected surprise.

1025
01:10:56.486 --> 01:11:00.057
The police have raided my home
in search of Igor Straussman.

1026
01:11:00.090 --> 01:11:02.225
We managed to avoid
incarceration, but...

1027
01:11:02.259 --> 01:11:04.227
...it's just possible
we might have

1028
01:11:04.261 --> 01:11:06.997
gravely wounded
a police officer.

1029
01:11:07.030 --> 01:11:10.133
Ah. I suppose now you'll have
no choice but to leave London.

1030
01:11:10.167 --> 01:11:12.102
Posthaste.
Very good.

1031
01:11:12.135 --> 01:11:13.403
My family has an estate.

1032
01:11:13.437 --> 01:11:15.705
The Castle Erskine
in Scotland. It's quite...

1033
01:11:16.606 --> 01:11:18.041
...rural and secluded.

1034
01:11:18.075 --> 01:11:19.843
Ideally situated,
you might say, for...

1035
01:11:19.876 --> 01:11:21.845
...both your needs
as scientists and, um...

1036
01:11:22.646 --> 01:11:23.713
...well, fugitives.

1037
01:11:24.014 --> 01:11:25.315
Yes.

1038
01:11:25.348 --> 01:11:27.184
I'll go and prepare the coach.

1039
01:11:28.151 --> 01:11:29.719
Very good, thank you!

1040
01:11:31.021 --> 01:11:33.223
How could you do that to me?
Do what?

1041
01:11:33.256 --> 01:11:34.724
Keep from me
that you had killed a man

1042
01:11:34.758 --> 01:11:36.093
and given me his name!

1043
01:11:36.126 --> 01:11:37.627
I told you,
I did not kill Straussman.

1044
01:11:37.661 --> 01:11:38.661
You're overreacting.

1045
01:11:38.995 --> 01:11:40.363
You harvested his eyes!

1046
01:11:40.397 --> 01:11:41.798
Details.

1047
01:11:41.832 --> 01:11:43.099
He was a waste of space.

1048
01:11:43.133 --> 01:11:45.168
This fanfare from you

1049
01:11:45.202 --> 01:11:46.937
is more than his own family
will give him.

1050
01:11:46.970 --> 01:11:48.472
All right, gentlemen,

1051
01:11:48.505 --> 01:11:50.225
time is of the essence.
Your coach is ready.

1052
01:11:50.707 --> 01:11:52.409
Come, Igor.

1053
01:11:52.442 --> 01:11:53.410
We'll talk about this
on the way.

1054
01:11:53.443 --> 01:11:54.478
No.

1055
01:11:55.011 --> 01:11:56.446
What?

1056
01:11:56.480 --> 01:11:58.148
What you're doing is wrong.

1057
01:11:59.316 --> 01:12:00.750
You've gone mad. Come.

1058
01:12:00.784 --> 01:12:02.285
It's gone too far.

1059
01:12:02.319 --> 01:12:04.287
We simply
do not have the time.

1060
01:12:05.322 --> 01:12:06.556
I'm not leaving then.

1061
01:12:08.258 --> 01:12:10.193
Listen to me.

1062
01:12:10.227 --> 01:12:11.928
You have the chance here
to be part of...

1063
01:12:11.962 --> 01:12:12.962
Of what?

1064
01:12:13.530 --> 01:12:15.632
Of being lied to by you?

1065
01:12:15.665 --> 01:12:18.602
Of being hunted by the police
and chased by monsters?

1066
01:12:18.635 --> 01:12:19.970
Well, if you're going
to concentrate

1067
01:12:20.003 --> 01:12:21.171
on the dark side.

1068
01:12:21.204 --> 01:12:23.173
I'm not leaving.

1069
01:12:23.206 --> 01:12:25.275
What will you do?
Go back to the circus?

1070
01:12:25.308 --> 01:12:26.476
Resurrect your
illustrious career as...

1071
01:12:26.510 --> 01:12:27.590
It's none of your concern.

1072
01:12:33.817 --> 01:12:35.318
You're a fool.

1073
01:12:39.656 --> 01:12:41.258
I created you.

1074
01:12:42.726 --> 01:12:44.461
You think that just because
I put you in a back brace

1075
01:12:44.494 --> 01:12:47.264
and you cut your hair...

1076
01:12:47.297 --> 01:12:48.865
...you can
turn your back on me?

1077
01:12:50.367 --> 01:12:52.736
That you can walk out
into the world on your own?

1078
01:12:53.670 --> 01:12:56.072
See how far you get
with your acrobat

1079
01:12:56.106 --> 01:12:57.674
and your morals
and your new life.

1080
01:12:58.308 --> 01:12:59.876
Just come with me.

1081
01:13:05.715 --> 01:13:06.715
Fine.

1082
01:13:10.187 --> 01:13:11.621
I'm done with you.

1083
01:13:37.981 --> 01:13:40.517
You know... I knew
Igor Straussman.

1084
01:13:42.586 --> 01:13:44.254
He was a real bore.

1085
01:13:44.988 --> 01:13:47.257
Nouveau riche. Drug addict.

1086
01:13:48.425 --> 01:13:49.926
So, who are you then?

1087
01:13:50.961 --> 01:13:51.961
Hmm?

1088
01:13:52.495 --> 01:13:53.930
Doesn't matter really.

1089
01:13:55.565 --> 01:13:58.201
Victor's been very forthcoming
with his designs.

1090
01:13:58.234 --> 01:13:59.736
But I still need him for now.

1091
01:14:02.272 --> 01:14:04.674
You, on the other hand...

1092
01:14:06.343 --> 01:14:10.647
So, let's see. Your benefactor
has departed...

1093
01:14:10.680 --> 01:14:13.550
...your home has been
ransacked by police...

1094
01:14:15.218 --> 01:14:18.788
...your identity
revealed as a fraud...

1095
01:14:18.822 --> 01:14:22.025
...and you know far too much
for me to let you walk away.

1096
01:14:24.494 --> 01:14:26.062
What I'm getting at,
old boy...

1097
01:14:27.797 --> 01:14:29.157
...is that
you won't be missed.

1098
01:14:33.470 --> 01:14:35.070
Tie him up
and put him in the carriage.

1099
01:14:36.973 --> 01:14:39.013
<i>You and Victor aren't
the only ones with vision.</i>

1100
01:14:39.943 --> 01:14:42.345
I, too,
have a dream of the future.

1101
01:14:42.379 --> 01:14:44.180
<i>A dream where my family</i>

1102
01:14:44.214 --> 01:14:45.574
<i>will control
this new technology.</i>

1103
01:14:46.216 --> 01:14:47.717
Hmm? What's that?

1104
01:14:49.119 --> 01:14:50.787
<i>You don't approve.</i>

1105
01:14:50.820 --> 01:14:53.590
No, I imagined you and Victor
wouldn't like that much.

1106
01:14:54.624 --> 01:14:57.460
You know, for men
obsessed with death,

1107
01:14:57.494 --> 01:14:59.174
you think yourselves
so above violence.

1108
01:15:01.598 --> 01:15:02.732
Curious.

1109
01:15:04.267 --> 01:15:05.669
<i>Good-bye, Igor.</i>

1110
01:15:58.188 --> 01:15:59.856
Straussman wasn't Straussman.

1111
01:16:01.157 --> 01:16:03.893
The body, the frozen creature,
that was Straussman.

1112
01:16:03.927 --> 01:16:05.228
The young man pretending
to be Straussman

1113
01:16:05.261 --> 01:16:06.329
was the hunchback...

1114
01:16:06.362 --> 01:16:07.530
...transformed
by Frankenstein.

1115
01:16:07.564 --> 01:16:08.765
Inspector, this is not...

1116
01:16:08.798 --> 01:16:10.967
They escaped in the
Finnegan family coach.

1117
01:16:11.000 --> 01:16:12.469
Finnegan attends
the Royal College of Medicine.

1118
01:16:12.502 --> 01:16:14.170
It makes sense.

1119
01:16:14.204 --> 01:16:16.172
He's in on it, too,
maybe funding them.

1120
01:16:16.206 --> 01:16:17.240
Inspector Turpin, stop...

1121
01:16:17.273 --> 01:16:18.742
My guess is that
he's fled the country by now,

1122
01:16:18.775 --> 01:16:21.277
more than likely
alongside Finnegan...

1123
01:16:21.311 --> 01:16:22.345
...who, a little digging
shows, has an estate,

1124
01:16:22.379 --> 01:16:24.514
Castle Erskine in Scotland.

1125
01:16:24.547 --> 01:16:25.982
We'll find them there.

1126
01:16:26.015 --> 01:16:27.350
Stop it, Roderick, damn it!

1127
01:16:27.384 --> 01:16:28.985
No, listen to me!

1128
01:16:29.018 --> 01:16:30.787
We can catch them now.

1129
01:16:31.888 --> 01:16:33.022
We can...

1130
01:16:33.923 --> 01:16:34.923
...and we will.

1131
01:16:39.596 --> 01:16:41.831
What do you mean?

1132
01:16:41.865 --> 01:16:44.434
You're being removed
from the case... sir.

1133
01:16:45.268 --> 01:16:47.537
From the whole force, in fact.

1134
01:16:47.570 --> 01:16:49.773
Constable Alistair will be
taking your place.

1135
01:16:49.806 --> 01:16:52.509
You are on a medical
and mental reprieve.

1136
01:16:54.444 --> 01:16:56.579
You had no warrant, Roderick.

1137
01:16:57.981 --> 01:17:00.183
Do you have any idea
the lengths I have been to...

1138
01:17:00.216 --> 01:17:02.652
...in order to protect you
from criminal charges?

1139
01:17:03.620 --> 01:17:05.722
It was a necessary action. Really?

1140
01:17:07.390 --> 01:17:08.925
In pursuit of what?

1141
01:17:10.693 --> 01:17:12.729
High society hunchbacks?

1142
01:17:13.563 --> 01:17:15.932
Undead monsters?

1143
01:17:17.233 --> 01:17:18.635
Conspiracies involving

1144
01:17:18.668 --> 01:17:20.437
one of the richest families
in England?

1145
01:17:20.470 --> 01:17:22.806
Yes, a conspiracy
to create life in...

1146
01:17:25.008 --> 01:17:28.077
...a direct, defiant action
against God.

1147
01:17:29.846 --> 01:17:32.448
You were the best detective
Scotland Yard had,

1148
01:17:32.482 --> 01:17:33.950
but now it's time
for you to rest.

1149
01:17:33.983 --> 01:17:35.952
You must heal.
And when you return,

1150
01:17:35.985 --> 01:17:38.221
you will see things
how they really are.

1151
01:18:26.536 --> 01:18:27.670
<i>Is that precious?</i>

1152
01:18:30.473 --> 01:18:32.942
I took possession of this
when I was... ten.

1153
01:18:34.544 --> 01:18:36.913
It was a very cold winter
that year.

1154
01:18:36.946 --> 01:18:39.048
We lived in the country then.
It was a happy time.

1155
01:18:39.949 --> 01:18:41.784
We crept out of
my bedroom window

1156
01:18:41.818 --> 01:18:42.652
because we wanted to
play in the snow...

1157
01:18:42.685 --> 01:18:43.887
...and so we did.

1158
01:18:45.088 --> 01:18:46.289
Until we were...

1159
01:18:47.557 --> 01:18:49.158
...engulfed by a blizzard.

1160
01:18:51.394 --> 01:18:52.962
I almost died.

1161
01:18:54.631 --> 01:18:56.399
Anyway, when...

1162
01:18:56.432 --> 01:18:57.767
When the snow cleared...

1163
01:18:58.868 --> 01:19:00.703
...and dawn finally broke...

1164
01:19:02.505 --> 01:19:03.907
...I was alive.

1165
01:19:07.577 --> 01:19:09.712
I looked into my hand
and I was holding this.

1166
01:19:11.581 --> 01:19:13.116
It serves to remind me.

1167
01:19:15.518 --> 01:19:17.053
Remind you of what?

1168
01:19:18.688 --> 01:19:19.989
That God...

1169
01:19:23.226 --> 01:19:24.928
...if at all He does exist...

1170
01:19:27.130 --> 01:19:29.933
...sent us
into this world imperfect.

1171
01:19:32.368 --> 01:19:33.803
We're weak.

1172
01:19:34.504 --> 01:19:35.939
We're fragile.

1173
01:19:37.807 --> 01:19:39.342
And we're destined to die.

1174
01:19:43.880 --> 01:19:46.015
This reminds me that
that is not good enough.

1175
01:19:47.483 --> 01:19:48.885
Who were you with?

1176
01:19:49.585 --> 01:19:50.620
Hmm?

1177
01:19:51.888 --> 01:19:53.957
You said "we".
In the blizzard.

1178
01:19:54.290 --> 01:19:55.290
Did I?

1179
01:20:14.510 --> 01:20:17.180
Where in God's name
do you think you're going?

1180
01:20:17.213 --> 01:20:18.653
You haven't been
out of bed in weeks!

1181
01:20:18.681 --> 01:20:20.049
You can barely walk!

1182
01:20:21.117 --> 01:20:23.853
Igor. Igor, don't go.
Don't do this.

1183
01:20:23.886 --> 01:20:25.822
I have to go. He needs me.

1184
01:20:27.156 --> 01:20:28.324
You owe him nothing.

1185
01:20:29.325 --> 01:20:30.093
You're your own man.

1186
01:20:30.326 --> 01:20:31.326
No.

1187
01:20:31.894 --> 01:20:33.396
I'm the man he made me.

1188
01:20:34.630 --> 01:20:35.932
You're wrong.

1189
01:20:37.033 --> 01:20:39.168
You've always been
this person.

1190
01:20:39.202 --> 01:20:41.337
This brave,
brilliant, beautiful person.

1191
01:20:41.804 --> 01:20:43.873
He gave me a life.

1192
01:20:46.342 --> 01:20:48.144
I'm sorry, Lorelei, but...

1193
01:20:48.978 --> 01:20:51.214
...you must understand,
I have to go.

1194
01:20:52.515 --> 01:20:54.017
He's my friend.

1195
01:20:56.719 --> 01:20:58.421
Then you will not go alone.

1196
01:21:10.767 --> 01:21:12.602
<i>Two hearts.</i>

1197
01:21:12.635 --> 01:21:14.437
<i>Pump all that blood
around the larger body.</i>

1198
01:21:18.975 --> 01:21:22.712
<i>A larger chest cavity
to incorporate four lungs.</i>

1199
01:21:22.745 --> 01:21:24.781
<i>Two sets on the left
and the right.</i>

1200
01:21:38.161 --> 01:21:40.563
<i>You and I, Igor...
we shall create a man...</i>

1201
01:21:40.596 --> 01:21:42.999
<i>...after our own image.</i>

1202
01:21:49.739 --> 01:21:51.140
<i>An intelligent...</i>

1203
01:21:51.607 --> 01:21:53.276
<i>...civilized...</i>

1204
01:21:53.676 --> 01:21:55.344
<i>...man.</i>

1205
01:22:14.664 --> 01:22:15.765
Stop!

1206
01:22:17.733 --> 01:22:19.268
- Stop here!
- Whoa!

1207
01:22:24.874 --> 01:22:26.109
Finnegan's men.

1208
01:22:27.543 --> 01:22:28.543
Wait here.

1209
01:22:32.749 --> 01:22:34.117
Please take care.

1210
01:22:38.187 --> 01:22:40.123
What are you doing?
Go.

1211
01:22:55.238 --> 01:22:56.272
Hello?

1212
01:22:57.473 --> 01:22:59.208
Sorry, we seem to be lost.

1213
01:23:06.582 --> 01:23:07.884
Thank you!

1214
01:23:20.196 --> 01:23:21.230
What's this?

1215
01:23:42.618 --> 01:23:44.554
Hold her here.
I'm going to the castle.

1216
01:23:44.587 --> 01:23:47.056
Sir, there is a storm coming.

1217
01:23:47.089 --> 01:23:50.593
That man is in allegiance with
Satan... and must be stopped!

1218
01:24:09.412 --> 01:24:11.347
All stations ready!

1219
01:24:11.380 --> 01:24:14.750
Engineers! Scientists!
Eyes to me!

1220
01:24:14.784 --> 01:24:17.053
The storm is nigh!

1221
01:24:17.086 --> 01:24:21.891
The storm is nigh!
Conditions are perfect!

1222
01:24:25.895 --> 01:24:29.031
Electrical station
ready, sir!

1223
01:24:33.436 --> 01:24:36.239
Prometheus moving,
station one!

1224
01:24:43.346 --> 01:24:46.282
Stoke the furnace!
We need it hotter!

1225
01:24:46.315 --> 01:24:47.635
Mind the blood pipe!

1226
01:24:53.623 --> 01:24:55.258
Prepare the blood!

1227
01:24:55.291 --> 01:24:57.193
Fluid station now!

1228
01:24:58.694 --> 01:25:00.196
Now. Set?

1229
01:25:01.764 --> 01:25:03.266
Inserting.

1230
01:25:03.299 --> 01:25:05.101
In. Tapped.

1231
01:25:13.843 --> 01:25:16.946
Respiratory station!

1232
01:25:16.979 --> 01:25:19.081
Prepare
the respiratory station!

1233
01:25:20.616 --> 01:25:21.617
Victor.

1234
01:25:22.852 --> 01:25:24.654
Igor?

1235
01:25:24.687 --> 01:25:26.522
I'm so glad you've come.

1236
01:25:26.555 --> 01:25:28.958
Victor, Finnegan tried to
have me killed.

1237
01:25:28.991 --> 01:25:30.926
I believe he intends to
kill you, too,

1238
01:25:30.960 --> 01:25:33.195
when you've given him
what he wants.

1239
01:25:33.229 --> 01:25:35.197
We can still get out of this,

1240
01:25:35.231 --> 01:25:36.699
but you must stop
this experiment.

1241
01:25:36.732 --> 01:25:38.000
Father sent you, didn't he?

1242
01:25:38.034 --> 01:25:39.502
Don't be ridiculous!

1243
01:25:39.535 --> 01:25:40.870
He'll stop at nothing,

1244
01:25:40.903 --> 01:25:42.543
and you don't know
what he's capable of!

1245
01:25:43.773 --> 01:25:44.874
I don't care.

1246
01:25:44.907 --> 01:25:46.442
What?

1247
01:25:46.475 --> 01:25:48.678
Finnegan's motives
mean nothing to me.

1248
01:25:48.711 --> 01:25:52.181
I will turn the tide of human
existence here, tonight.

1249
01:25:52.214 --> 01:25:55.284
Then this world
which has spurned me...

1250
01:25:55.318 --> 01:25:57.920
...will forever
remember my name!

1251
01:25:57.954 --> 01:25:59.422
No, if you do what he asks,

1252
01:25:59.455 --> 01:26:01.357
no one will remember
Frankenstein the man.

1253
01:26:01.390 --> 01:26:02.658
Only the monster!

1254
01:26:06.028 --> 01:26:08.497
I forgive you, Igor.

1255
01:26:08.531 --> 01:26:10.700
I forgive you this remarkable
lack of foresight.

1256
01:26:10.733 --> 01:26:12.101
So stay here!

1257
01:26:12.969 --> 01:26:14.503
Your brother was with you!

1258
01:26:16.005 --> 01:26:17.907
Henry Frankenstein.

1259
01:26:17.940 --> 01:26:19.408
He was with you that night.

1260
01:26:20.977 --> 01:26:22.545
Was he older
or younger than you?

1261
01:26:23.379 --> 01:26:25.114
He was older.

1262
01:26:25.147 --> 01:26:26.749
You must have
looked up to him.

1263
01:26:30.219 --> 01:26:32.088
Where did you get that?

1264
01:26:32.121 --> 01:26:33.456
I wouldn't be surprised

1265
01:26:33.489 --> 01:26:35.791
if it was your idea, though.
Was it?

1266
01:26:35.825 --> 01:26:38.227
To go out into the snow.
And he protected you.

1267
01:26:39.228 --> 01:26:41.297
And he died while you lived.

1268
01:26:44.066 --> 01:26:46.235
Isn't that what
all this is about, Victor?

1269
01:26:47.136 --> 01:26:49.372
You want to stop
other people...

1270
01:26:49.405 --> 01:26:51.574
...from having to endure
that pain that you felt.

1271
01:26:56.312 --> 01:26:57.312
No.

1272
01:26:57.546 --> 01:26:58.546
No?

1273
01:27:00.850 --> 01:27:02.118
No.

1274
01:27:06.222 --> 01:27:08.391
It's about so much
more than that.

1275
01:27:11.027 --> 01:27:14.196
Don't you see? To my mind...

1276
01:27:14.230 --> 01:27:15.731
I took my brother's life
that night.

1277
01:27:20.102 --> 01:27:22.538
I have to redress the balance.

1278
01:27:25.141 --> 01:27:28.210
I have to create life now.

1279
01:27:29.678 --> 01:27:33.816
Victor, none of this
does that.

1280
01:27:33.849 --> 01:27:38.254
This only brings
more and more and more pain.

1281
01:27:40.356 --> 01:27:42.558
And whatever path this is
that you've gone down,

1282
01:27:42.591 --> 01:27:44.160
this is not you.

1283
01:27:44.960 --> 01:27:47.229
You're a good man, Victor.

1284
01:27:58.240 --> 01:28:00.443
- Igor...
- Frankenstein!

1285
01:28:00.476 --> 01:28:03.446
Frankenstein! Hurry, man!
The storm is almost upon us!

1286
01:28:06.515 --> 01:28:07.516
Victor...

1287
01:28:07.950 --> 01:28:09.251
...don't.

1288
01:28:13.489 --> 01:28:14.657
Victor!

1289
01:28:20.129 --> 01:28:22.565
Station one ready!

1290
01:28:31.574 --> 01:28:33.175
Prometheus moving!

1291
01:28:35.778 --> 01:28:38.214
Electrical station!

1292
01:28:38.247 --> 01:28:40.549
Electrical station
ready, sir!

1293
01:28:54.363 --> 01:28:56.265
Who'd have thought it, eh?

1294
01:28:56.298 --> 01:28:59.468
You and I on the threshold
of immortality.

1295
01:29:04.707 --> 01:29:06.809
Prometheus moving!

1296
01:29:07.209 --> 01:29:08.777
Lazarus station!

1297
01:29:09.311 --> 01:29:10.813
Damn them all, eh?

1298
01:29:11.780 --> 01:29:14.817
The naysayers... and
the hypocrites.

1299
01:29:20.422 --> 01:29:22.658
For tonight, Victor,
we breathe life...

1300
01:29:23.092 --> 01:29:24.660
...into flesh!

1301
01:29:30.132 --> 01:29:32.234
Balloons released!

1302
01:29:51.053 --> 01:29:52.454
Lazarus Fork.

1303
01:30:00.462 --> 01:30:02.932
I will give you life.

1304
01:30:03.666 --> 01:30:05.267
I will give you...

1305
01:30:05.701 --> 01:30:06.701
...life!

1306
01:30:10.873 --> 01:30:14.009
Prometheus ascending!

1307
01:30:27.156 --> 01:30:28.557
Station ready, sir!

1308
01:30:29.558 --> 01:30:31.594
I want full power,
on my mark.

1309
01:30:31.627 --> 01:30:32.627
Now!

1310
01:30:33.529 --> 01:30:36.298
Converter B standing by.

1311
01:30:36.332 --> 01:30:37.700
Full power... now!

1312
01:30:41.203 --> 01:30:43.038
All positions, relays open!

1313
01:30:49.411 --> 01:30:50.980
This is your moment, Victor!

1314
01:30:51.647 --> 01:30:52.647
Victor!

1315
01:30:53.182 --> 01:30:54.650
It's too much power!

1316
01:30:57.653 --> 01:30:59.054
<i>You know this story.</i>

1317
01:31:01.991 --> 01:31:03.325
<i>The crack of lightning.</i>

1318
01:31:04.994 --> 01:31:06.729
<i>A mad genius.</i>

1319
01:31:09.565 --> 01:31:11.300
<i>An unholy creation.</i>

1320
01:31:12.368 --> 01:31:13.402
Victor...

1321
01:31:15.404 --> 01:31:16.438
...don't!

1322
01:31:18.207 --> 01:31:21.076
Live!

1323
01:32:05.187 --> 01:32:06.388
Well, Victor.

1324
01:32:10.959 --> 01:32:12.361
Sir, I must warn you...

1325
01:32:15.197 --> 01:32:16.865
...we are overloading!

1326
01:32:35.684 --> 01:32:36.785
No!

1327
01:32:47.196 --> 01:32:48.764
No!

1328
01:33:38.914 --> 01:33:40.482
Frankenstein!

1329
01:33:43.419 --> 01:33:46.255
You will burn
for what you do here.

1330
01:33:46.288 --> 01:33:48.390
This isn't science.

1331
01:33:48.424 --> 01:33:49.824
This is the work
of Satan himself.

1332
01:33:54.463 --> 01:33:58.901
There's no Satan.
No God. Only humanity.

1333
01:33:59.301 --> 01:34:00.869
Only me!

1334
01:34:32.601 --> 01:34:34.069
May God forgive you,
Frankenstein!

1335
01:34:34.102 --> 01:34:35.971
May God forgive you!

1336
01:35:02.264 --> 01:35:03.765
Out of the way, Victor!

1337
01:35:04.233 --> 01:35:05.634
Out of the way!

1338
01:35:06.168 --> 01:35:07.603
Come to me.

1339
01:35:13.075 --> 01:35:14.610
I am your brother.

1340
01:35:59.855 --> 01:36:01.957
Oh, my brother Henry,
forgive me.

1341
01:36:05.594 --> 01:36:07.229
I have wronged you.

1342
01:36:09.197 --> 01:36:11.099
For this is not life.

1343
01:36:13.335 --> 01:36:15.938
This is not life!

1344
01:36:18.040 --> 01:36:20.208
You are not life!

1345
01:36:20.575 --> 01:36:22.110
Live!

1346
01:36:22.144 --> 01:36:24.279
Victor!
Out of the way, Frankenstein!

1347
01:36:24.313 --> 01:36:26.214
Live! Live! Live!

1348
01:36:45.200 --> 01:36:47.502
May God drive out
this devil...

1349
01:36:47.536 --> 01:36:49.204
...and be driven back
to the pits of hell

1350
01:36:49.237 --> 01:36:50.237
from whence he came.

1351
01:36:54.242 --> 01:36:55.410
No!

1352
01:37:33.281 --> 01:37:36.284
Igor, I'm sorry.
What are we going to do?

1353
01:37:36.318 --> 01:37:37.819
What are we going to do now?

1354
01:37:41.857 --> 01:37:44.459
We will do the only thing
we can do.

1355
01:37:55.670 --> 01:37:56.772
Huh?

1356
01:38:09.451 --> 01:38:10.452
Shit.

1357
01:38:30.205 --> 01:38:31.239
No!

1358
01:39:08.643 --> 01:39:09.643
Igor!

1359
01:39:24.793 --> 01:39:26.261
Victor...

1360
01:39:27.162 --> 01:39:28.163
...get off.

1361
01:40:05.267 --> 01:40:06.568
Igor!

1362
01:40:08.003 --> 01:40:09.337
Two hearts!

1363
01:40:11.173 --> 01:40:12.474
No!

1364
01:40:43.638 --> 01:40:46.141
Oh, my brother, forgive me!

1365
01:41:54.910 --> 01:41:56.144
Victor?

1366
01:42:43.258 --> 01:42:45.026
<i>Dearest Igor:</i>

1367
01:42:45.060 --> 01:42:47.062
<i>I would have
waited for you, but...</i>

1368
01:42:47.095 --> 01:42:48.897
<i>...three's a crowd
and all that.</i>

1369
01:42:48.930 --> 01:42:50.398
<i>Besides, I think</i>

1370
01:42:50.432 --> 01:42:52.072
<i>you've probably had enough
of my work.</i>

1371
01:42:52.100 --> 01:42:53.980
<i>Truth be told, you've probably
had enough of me.</i>

1372
01:42:55.170 --> 01:42:56.438
<i>Our time together is done.</i>

1373
01:42:56.471 --> 01:42:58.139
<i>Our achievements
are in the past...</i>

1374
01:42:58.173 --> 01:43:01.176
<i>...and our discoveries
will probably never be known.</i>

1375
01:43:01.209 --> 01:43:02.977
<i>But I will always
think of you fondly,</i>

1376
01:43:03.011 --> 01:43:05.313
<i>and always as my friend.</i>

1377
01:43:05.914 --> 01:43:07.682
<i>As for myself...</i>

1378
01:43:07.716 --> 01:43:09.217
<i>...I have some ideas</i>

1379
01:43:09.250 --> 01:43:11.052
<i>about where we went wrong
this time...</i>

1380
01:43:11.086 --> 01:43:13.355
<i>...and one day I may
call on you once more.</i>

1381
01:43:13.788 --> 01:43:15.457
<i>Be ready.</i>

1382
01:43:15.490 --> 01:43:18.593
<i>For now,
your life is your own...</i>

1383
01:43:18.626 --> 01:43:20.495
<i>...and I wish you
luck with it.</i>

1384
01:43:22.230 --> 01:43:25.633
<i>You are and will remain
my greatest creation.</i>

1385
01:43:27.435 --> 01:43:28.503
<i>Your friend...</i>
